DATA.push({"c":"toeic","l":3,"w":[["comply","/kəmˈplaɪ/","v.","遵守","All products must comply with safety standards.","所有產品都必須符合安全標準。"],["liability","/ˌlaɪəˈbɪləti/","n.","（法律）責任；負債","The company accepts no liability for lost items.","公司對遺失物品不負責任。"],["consolidate","/kənˈsɑːlɪdeɪt/","v.","合併、整合","We plan to consolidate the two warehouses.","我們計畫把兩個倉庫合併。"],["streamline","/ˈstriːmlaɪn/","v.","精簡、使有效率","The new system will streamline the ordering process.","新系統會簡化訂購流程。"],["expedite","/ˈekspədaɪt/","v.","加快處理","Could you expedite the shipment?","可以加快出貨嗎？"],["tentative","/ˈtentətɪv/","adj.","暫定的","The meeting is tentatively set for Monday.","會議暫定週一。"],["preliminary","/prɪˈlɪmɪneri/","adj.","初步的","The preliminary results look promising.","初步結果看起來不錯。"],["discrepancy","/dɪˈskrepənsi/","n.","差異、不符","There is a discrepancy between the invoice and the order.","發票和訂單有出入。"],["incentive","/ɪnˈsentɪv/","n.","獎勵、誘因","Sales staff receive a bonus as an incentive.","業務人員有獎金當作獎勵。"],["prospective","/prəˈspektɪv/","adj.","潛在的、未來的","We're meeting a prospective client tomorrow.","我們明天要見一位潛在客戶。"],["lucrative","/ˈluːkrətɪv/","adj.","有利可圖的","It's a lucrative market.","這是個很賺錢的市場。"],["feasible","/ˈfiːzəbl/","adj.","可行的","Is this plan financially feasible?","這個計畫在財務上可行嗎？"],["adjacent","/əˈdʒeɪsnt/","adj.","鄰近的","Parking is available in the adjacent building.","隔壁大樓可以停車。"],["commence","/kəˈmens/","v.","開始","Construction will commence in June.","工程將於六月開始。"],["adhere to","/ədˈhɪr tuː/","phr.","遵守、堅持","Staff must adhere to the dress code.","員工必須遵守服裝規定。"],["in accordance with","/ɪn əˈkɔːrdns wɪð/","phr.","依照","Refunds are issued in accordance with our policy.","退款依照本公司規定辦理。"],["mandatory","/ˈmændətɔːri/","adj.","強制的","Attendance at the training is mandatory.","訓練一定要出席。"],["outsource","/ˈaʊtsɔːrs/","v.","外包","We outsource our IT support.","我們把 IT 支援外包出去。"],["acquisition","/ˌækwɪˈzɪʃən/","n.","收購","The acquisition was completed last month.","收購案上個月完成。"],["merger","/ˈmɝːdʒɚ/","n.","（公司）合併","The merger created the largest firm in the industry.","這次合併造就了業界最大的公司。"],["stakeholder","/ˈsteɪkhoʊldɚ/","n.","利害關係人","We need approval from all stakeholders.","我們需要所有利害關係人同意。"],["endorse","/ɪnˈdɔːrs/","v.","背書、支持","The board endorsed the new strategy.","董事會支持新策略。"],["forfeit","/ˈfɔːrfɪt/","v.","喪失（權利等）","If you cancel late, you forfeit the deposit.","太晚取消會沒收訂金。"],["substantial","/səbˈstænʃl/","adj.","大量的、可觀的","We saw a substantial increase in sales.","銷售大幅成長。"],["accommodate","/əˈkɑːmədeɪt/","v.","容納；配合","The room can accommodate 50 people.","這個房間可容納 50 人。"],["itemize","/ˈaɪtəmaɪz/","v.","逐項列出","Please itemize all expenses.","請逐項列出所有費用。"],["reconcile","/ˈrekənsaɪl/","v.","核對（帳目）；調和","We reconcile the accounts every month.","我們每個月對帳。"],["probationary","/proʊˈbeɪʃəneri/","adj.","試用期的","New hires have a three-month probationary period.","新進員工有三個月試用期。"],["unanimous","/juˈnænɪməs/","adj.","一致同意的","The decision was unanimous.","這個決定全體一致通過。"],["deem","/diːm/","v.","認為、視為","The project was deemed a success.","這個專案被視為成功。"],["recruitment drive","/rɪˈkruːtmənt ˌdraɪv/","phr.","招募活動","The bank launched a recruitment drive for graduates.","銀行針對畢業生展開招募活動。"],["headhunt","/ˈhedhʌnt/","v.","挖角、獵才","She was headhunted by a rival firm.","她被競爭對手公司挖角。"],["poach","/poʊtʃ/","v.","挖角","Competitors tried to poach our top engineers.","競爭對手試圖挖走我們的頂尖工程師。"],["talent pool","/ˈtælənt ˌpuːl/","phr.","人才庫","We keep strong applicants in our talent pool.","我們把優秀的應徵者留在人才庫中。"],["aptitude test","/ˈæptɪtuːd ˌtest/","phr.","性向測驗","Applicants must pass an aptitude test.","應徵者必須通過性向測驗。"],["competency","/ˈkɑːmpɪtənsi/","n.","能力、勝任力","The interview tests key competencies.","面試會測試關鍵能力。"],["caliber","/ˈkæləbər/","n.","（人的）素質、才幹","We attract candidates of high caliber.","我們吸引高素質的應徵者。"],["well-qualified","/ˌwel ˈkwɑːləfaɪd/","adj.","條件很好的","She is well-qualified for the managerial role.","她非常符合管理職的條件。"],["overqualified","/ˌoʊvərˈkwɑːləfaɪd/","adj.","資歷過高的","He was considered overqualified for the job.","他被認為資歷過高而不適任。"],["underqualified","/ˌʌndərˈkwɑːləfaɪd/","adj.","資格不足的","Some applicants were underqualified.","有些應徵者資格不足。"],["prerequisite","/priːˈrekwəzɪt/","n.","先決條件","A master's degree is a prerequisite.","碩士學位是先決條件。"],["track record","/ˈtræk ˌrekərd/","phr.","過往績效紀錄","She has a proven track record in sales.","她在業務方面有亮眼的績效紀錄。"],["accomplishment","/əˈkɑːmplɪʃmənt/","n.","成就","List your main accomplishments on your resume.","請在履歷中列出你的主要成就。"],["transferable skills","/trænsˈfɝːəbəl ˌskɪlz/","phr.","可轉移技能","Teaching gave her many transferable skills.","教書經驗給了她許多可轉移的技能。"],["employment contract","/ɪmˈplɔɪmənt ˌkɑːntrækt/","phr.","僱傭合約","Read the employment contract before signing.","簽署前請詳讀僱傭合約。"],["offer letter","/ˈɔːfər ˌletər/","phr.","錄取通知書","The offer letter states your salary.","錄取通知書載明你的薪資。"],["counteroffer","/ˈkaʊntərˌɔːfər/","n.","反提議、還價","She received a counteroffer from her current employer.","她收到現任雇主的慰留條件。"],["negotiable","/nɪˈgoʊʃiəbəl/","adj.","可協商的","The salary is negotiable for the right person.","適合的人選薪資可議。"],["commensurate with","/kəˈmenʃərət wɪð/","phr.","與……相稱","Salary will be commensurate with experience.","薪資將依經驗而定。"],["hiring manager","/ˈhaɪərɪŋ ˌmænɪdʒər/","phr.","用人主管","The hiring manager makes the final decision.","由用人主管做最後決定。"],["induction","/ɪnˈdʌkʃən/","n.","新人引導、到職訓練","The induction covers company history and values.","到職訓練涵蓋公司歷史與價值觀。"],["probationary period","/proʊˈbeɪʃəneri ˌpɪriəd/","phr.","試用期","Benefits begin after the probationary period.","試用期過後開始享有福利。"],["apprentice","/əˈprentɪs/","n.","學徒","The apprentice learns from a senior technician.","學徒向資深技師學習。"],["apprenticeship","/əˈprentɪsʃɪp/","n.","學徒制","He completed a three-year apprenticeship.","他完成了三年的學徒訓練。"],["refresher course","/rɪˈfreʃər ˌkɔːrs/","phr.","進修課程","All drivers take a refresher course yearly.","所有司機每年都要上進修課程。"],["in-house training","/ˌɪn haʊs ˈtreɪnɪŋ/","phr.","內部訓練","We provide in-house training on safety.","我們提供安全方面的內部訓練。"],["upskill","/ˈʌpskɪl/","v.","提升技能","The company plans to upskill its workforce.","公司計畫提升員工的技能。"],["certification","/ˌsɝːtɪfɪˈkeɪʃən/","n.","認證、證照","The course leads to an official certification.","完成課程可取得正式認證。"],["accredited","/əˈkredɪtɪd/","adj.","經認可的","Only accredited trainers may teach this course.","只有經認可的講師能教授此課程。"],["module","/ˈmɑːdʒuːl/","n.","單元、模組","Complete each online module by Friday.","請在週五前完成每個線上單元。"],["e-learning","/ˈiː ˌlɝːnɪŋ/","n.","線上學習","Our e-learning platform is open all day.","我們的線上學習平台全天開放。"],["tuition reimbursement","/tuˈɪʃən ˌriːɪmˈbɝːsmənt/","phr.","學費補助","We offer tuition reimbursement for job-related courses.","我們為工作相關課程提供學費補助。"],["appraise","/əˈpreɪz/","v.","評估、考核","Managers appraise staff twice a year.","主管每年考核員工兩次。"],["performance appraisal","/pərˈfɔːrməns əˌpreɪzəl/","phr.","績效考核","Performance appraisals are held in December.","績效考核於十二月舉行。"],["key performance indicator","/ˌkiː pərˈfɔːrməns ˈɪndɪkeɪtər/","phr.","關鍵績效指標","Each team sets its own key performance indicators.","每個團隊設定自己的關鍵績效指標。"],["merit increase","/ˈmerɪt ˌɪnkriːs/","phr.","績效加薪","She received a merit increase this year.","她今年獲得績效加薪。"],["commend","/kəˈmend/","v.","稱讚、表揚","The manager commended her for her quick response.","經理表揚她反應迅速。"],["commendation","/ˌkɑːmenˈdeɪʃən/","n.","表揚","He received a commendation from the director.","他獲得處長的表揚。"],["reprimand","/ˈreprɪmænd/","n./v.","斥責、懲戒","He was reprimanded for missing the deadline.","他因錯過截止期限而遭斥責。"],["disciplinary action","/ˈdɪsəplɪneri ˈækʃən/","phr.","懲戒處分","Repeated lateness may lead to disciplinary action.","一再遲到可能導致懲戒處分。"],["misconduct","/ˌmɪsˈkɑːndʌkt/","n.","不當行為","He was dismissed for serious misconduct.","他因嚴重不當行為被解雇。"],["grievance procedure","/ˈgriːvəns prəˌsiːdʒər/","phr.","申訴程序","The handbook explains the grievance procedure.","員工手冊說明了申訴程序。"],["harassment","/həˈræsmənt/","n.","騷擾","The company has a strict policy against harassment.","公司對騷擾行為有嚴格政策。"],["discrimination","/dɪˌskrɪmɪˈneɪʃən/","n.","歧視","We do not tolerate discrimination of any kind.","我們不容許任何形式的歧視。"],["equal opportunity employer","/ˈiːkwəl ˌɑːpərˈtuːnəti ɪmˈplɔɪər/","phr.","機會平等雇主","We are an equal opportunity employer.","我們是提供平等就業機會的雇主。"],["inclusive","/ɪnˈkluːsɪv/","adj.","包容的","We aim to build an inclusive workplace.","我們致力打造包容的職場。"],["succession planning","/səkˈseʃən ˌplænɪŋ/","phr.","接班人規劃","Succession planning is a priority for the board.","接班人規劃是董事會的優先事項。"],["reassign","/ˌriːəˈsaɪn/","v.","重新分派","She was reassigned to the Taichung branch.","她被調派到台中分公司。"],["expatriate","/ekˈspeɪtriət/","n.","外派人員","Expatriates receive a housing allowance.","外派人員享有住房津貼。"],["relocation package","/ˌriːloʊˈkeɪʃən ˌpækɪdʒ/","phr.","搬遷補助方案","The relocation package covers moving costs.","搬遷補助方案涵蓋搬家費用。"],["voluntary","/ˈvɑːlənteri/","adj.","自願的","The company offered voluntary early retirement.","公司提供自願提前退休方案。"],["early retirement","/ˌɝːli rɪˈtaɪərmənt/","phr.","提早退休","He chose early retirement at fifty-five.","他選擇在五十五歲提早退休。"],["retiree","/rɪˌtaɪəˈriː/","n.","退休人員","Retirees keep their health insurance.","退休人員保留健康保險。"],["severance pay","/ˈsevərəns ˌpeɪ/","phr.","資遣費","Laid-off workers will receive severance pay.","被裁員工將獲得資遣費。"],["furlough","/ˈfɝːloʊ/","n./v.","無薪休假；暫時停職","Hundreds of workers were furloughed last year.","去年有數百名員工被要求無薪休假。"],["downsizing","/ˈdaʊnsaɪzɪŋ/","n.","裁員、縮編","Downsizing affected two departments.","縮編影響了兩個部門。"],["labor union","/ˈleɪbər ˌjuːnjən/","phr.","工會","The labor union met with management today.","工會今天與管理層會面。"],["collective bargaining","/kəˌlektɪv ˈbɑːrgənɪŋ/","phr.","集體協商","Wages are set through collective bargaining.","薪資透過集體協商決定。"],["strike","/straɪk/","n./v.","罷工","Workers went on strike for higher pay.","工人為了加薪而罷工。"],["employee retention","/ɪmˈplɔɪiː rɪˈtenʃən/","phr.","員工留任","Good benefits improve employee retention.","良好的福利能提升員工留任率。"],["attrition rate","/əˈtrɪʃən ˌreɪt/","phr.","人員流失率","Our attrition rate fell to five percent.","我們的人員流失率降到百分之五。"],["engagement","/ɪnˈgeɪdʒmənt/","n.","投入程度","Employee engagement rose after the survey.","調查後員工投入程度提升。"],["job security","/ˈdʒɑːb sɪˌkjʊrəti/","phr.","工作保障","Many workers value job security over salary.","許多員工重視工作保障甚於薪資。"],["burnout","/ˈbɝːnaʊt/","n.","過勞、倦怠","Long hours can lead to burnout.","長工時可能導致過勞。"],["compensation package","/ˌkɑːmpenˈseɪʃən ˌpækɪdʒ/","phr.","薪酬方案","The compensation package includes stock options.","薪酬方案包括股票選擇權。"],["pay stub","/ˈpeɪ ˌstʌb/","phr.","薪資明細","Keep your pay stubs for tax purposes.","請保留薪資明細以便報稅。"],["salaried","/ˈsælərid/","adj.","領月薪的","Salaried employees do not get overtime pay.","月薪制員工沒有加班費。"],["retroactive","/ˌretroʊˈæktɪv/","adj.","追溯的","The raise is retroactive to January.","加薪追溯至一月生效。"],["paid time off","/ˌpeɪd taɪm ˈɔːf/","phr.","帶薪休假","Employees earn paid time off each month.","員工每月累積帶薪休假。"],["sabbatical","/səˈbætɪkəl/","n.","長期休假、研修假","The professor is on sabbatical this year.","這位教授今年休研修假。"],["wellness program","/ˈwelnəs ˌproʊgræm/","phr.","健康促進計畫","Our wellness program includes free yoga classes.","我們的健康計畫包含免費瑜珈課。"],["on-site","/ˌɑːn ˈsaɪt/","adj.","現場的、公司內的","We have an on-site daycare center.","公司內設有托兒中心。"],["subsidized","/ˈsʌbsɪdaɪzd/","adj.","有補助的","Staff can eat subsidized meals in the cafeteria.","員工可在餐廳享用補助餐點。"],["eligibility","/ˌelɪdʒəˈbɪləti/","n.","資格","Check your eligibility for the bonus.","確認你是否有領獎金的資格。"],["entitlement","/ɪnˈtaɪtəlmənt/","n.","應享權利","Your leave entitlement is fifteen days.","你的應享假期為十五天。"],["administrative","/ədˈmɪnɪstreɪtɪv/","adj.","行政的","She handles administrative tasks for the team.","她負責團隊的行政工作。"],["administrator","/ədˈmɪnɪstreɪtər/","n.","管理員、行政人員","Contact the system administrator for access.","請聯絡系統管理員取得權限。"],["clerical","/ˈklerɪkəl/","adj.","文書的","The job involves clerical work and filing.","這份工作包含文書和歸檔。"],["filing","/ˈfaɪlɪŋ/","n.","歸檔","The intern spent the morning on filing.","實習生整個早上都在歸檔。"],["archive","/ˈɑːrkaɪv/","n./v.","檔案庫；存檔","Old emails are archived after one year.","舊郵件一年後會被存檔。"],["personnel file","/ˌpɝːsəˈnel ˌfaɪl/","phr.","人事檔案","Your review will be kept in your personnel file.","你的考核會存入人事檔案。"],["duplicate","/ˈduːplɪkət/","n./adj.","副本；重複的","Please make a duplicate of the signed contract.","請將簽好的合約複印一份。"],["countersign","/ˈkaʊntərsaɪn/","v.","會簽、副署","Your manager must countersign the request.","你的主管必須會簽此申請。"],["acknowledge receipt","/əkˈnɑːlɪdʒ rɪˈsiːt/","phr.","確認收到","Please acknowledge receipt of this letter.","請確認已收到此信。"],["heads-up","/ˈhedz ʌp/","n.","事先提醒","Thanks for the heads-up about the meeting.","謝謝你提醒我開會的事。"],["loop in","/ˌluːp ˈɪn/","phr.","讓……參與、知會","Please loop in the finance team on this.","這件事請知會財務團隊。"],["switchboard","/ˈswɪtʃbɔːrd/","n.","電話總機","Call the switchboard and ask for HR.","請打總機轉人資部。"],["operator","/ˈɑːpəreɪtər/","n.","接線生；操作員","The operator connected me to the right department.","接線生幫我轉到正確的部門。"],["teleconference","/ˈteləˌkɑːnfərəns/","n.","電話會議","The teleconference starts at eight a.m.","電話會議早上八點開始。"],["videoconference","/ˈvɪdioʊˌkɑːnfərəns/","n.","視訊會議","We held a videoconference with the Seoul office.","我們與首爾辦公室開了視訊會議。"],["reachable","/ˈriːtʃəbəl/","adj.","聯絡得到的","I'll be reachable by phone all day.","我整天都能用電話聯絡到。"],["prior engagement","/ˌpraɪər ɪnˈgeɪdʒmənt/","phr.","先前已有的約","Sorry, I have a prior engagement on Monday.","抱歉，我週一已經有約了。"],["scheduling conflict","/ˈskedʒuːlɪŋ ˌkɑːnflɪkt/","phr.","時間衝突","Due to a scheduling conflict, we must reschedule.","因時間衝突，我們必須改期。"],["availability","/əˌveɪləˈbɪləti/","n.","有空的時間；可用性","Please let me know your availability next week.","請告訴我你下週什麼時候有空。"],["pencil in","/ˌpensəl ˈɪn/","phr.","暫定（時間）","I'll pencil you in for Tuesday at two.","我先暫定您週二兩點。"],["no-show","/ˈnoʊ ʃoʊ/","n.","未到者、爽約","Two candidates were no-shows yesterday.","昨天有兩位候選人沒出現。"],["punctuality","/ˌpʌŋktʃuˈæləti/","n.","準時","Punctuality is expected of all employees.","所有員工都應準時。"],["workflow","/ˈwɝːkfloʊ/","n.","工作流程","The new software improved our workflow.","新軟體改善了我們的工作流程。"],["bureaucratic","/ˌbjʊrəˈkrætɪk/","adj.","官僚的","The approval process is too bureaucratic.","核准流程太官僚了。"],["red tape","/ˌred ˈteɪp/","phr.","繁文縟節","We cut a lot of red tape this year.","我們今年刪減了許多繁文縟節。"],["chain of command","/ˌtʃeɪn əv kəˈmænd/","phr.","指揮體系","Follow the chain of command when reporting problems.","回報問題時請遵循指揮體系。"],["line manager","/ˈlaɪn ˌmænɪdʒər/","phr.","直屬主管","Discuss leave with your line manager first.","請假前先跟直屬主管討論。"],["superior","/suːˈpɪriər/","n.","上司","Always inform your superior before leaving early.","提早離開前務必告知上司。"],["deputy","/ˈdepjəti/","n.","副手、代理人","The deputy manager will sign in my absence.","我不在時由副理簽核。"],["acting","/ˈæktɪŋ/","adj.","代理的","She is the acting head of HR.","她是人資部的代理主管。"],["interim","/ˈɪntərɪm/","adj.","臨時的、過渡的","An interim manager will run the office.","將由一位臨時經理管理辦公室。"],["vacate","/ˈveɪkeɪt/","v.","騰出（職位）","The post was vacated in March.","這個職位在三月出缺。"],["freelancer","/ˈfriːlænsər/","n.","自由工作者","We often use freelancers for translation.","我們常請自由工作者翻譯。"],["temp","/temp/","n.","臨時員工","A temp is covering the front desk this week.","這週由臨時員工負責櫃檯。"],["staffing agency","/ˈstæfɪŋ ˌeɪdʒənsi/","phr.","人力派遣公司","We hired temps through a staffing agency.","我們透過人力派遣公司找臨時員工。"],["vetting","/ˈvetɪŋ/","n.","審查、背景查核","All candidates go through a strict vetting process.","所有候選人都要經過嚴格的審查程序。"],["seasoned","/ˈsiːzənd/","adj.","經驗豐富的","We hired a seasoned HR director.","我們聘請了一位經驗豐富的人資總監。"],["veteran","/ˈvetərən/","n./adj.","老手；資深的","She is a veteran of the hotel industry.","她是飯店業的老手。"],["novice","/ˈnɑːvɪs/","n.","新手","The course is designed for novices.","這門課是為新手設計的。"],["designate","/ˈdezɪgneɪt/","v.","指派、指定","She was designated as the team's safety officer.","她被指派為團隊的安全負責人。"],["termination","/ˌtɝːmɪˈneɪʃən/","n.","終止；解雇","The contract allows termination with one month's notice.","合約允許提前一個月通知終止。"],["whistleblower","/ˈwɪsəlˌbloʊər/","n.","揭弊者","The policy protects whistleblowers.","這項政策保護揭弊者。"],["ergonomic","/ˌɝːgəˈnɑːmɪk/","adj.","符合人體工學的","We bought ergonomic chairs for all staff.","我們為全體員工購買人體工學椅。"],["occupational","/ˌɑːkjəˈpeɪʃənəl/","adj.","職業的","Occupational safety is our top priority.","職業安全是我們的首要考量。"],["occupation","/ˌɑːkjəˈpeɪʃən/","n.","職業","Please state your occupation on the form.","請在表格上填寫職業。"],["pay cut","/ˈpeɪ ˌkʌt/","phr.","減薪","Managers agreed to a ten percent pay cut.","經理們同意減薪百分之十。"],["hybrid work","/ˈhaɪbrɪd ˌwɝːk/","phr.","混合辦公","Our hybrid work model allows three office days.","我們的混合辦公模式為每週進辦公室三天。"],["dictate","/ˈdɪkteɪt/","v.","口述（讓人記錄）","The manager dictated a letter to his secretary.","經理口述一封信讓秘書記錄。"],["pertinent","/ˈpɝːtənənt/","adj.","相關的、切題的","Include only pertinent details in the memo.","備忘錄中只寫相關細節。"],["addressee","/ˌædreˈsiː/","n.","收信人","The addressee's name is spelled wrong.","收信人的名字拼錯了。"],["salutation","/ˌsæljəˈteɪʃən/","n.","（信件）稱呼語","Use a formal salutation such as \"Dear Sir.\"","請使用正式稱呼語，例如 \"Dear Sir\"。"],["enclosure","/ɪnˈkloʊʒər/","n.","（隨信）附件","The enclosure contains the training schedule.","隨附文件包含培訓時程表。"],["letterhead","/ˈleterhed/","n.","信紙抬頭","Print the offer on company letterhead.","請用公司信紙印製錄用通知。"],["reiterate","/riˈɪtəreɪt/","v.","重申","Let me reiterate the main points of the memo.","讓我重申備忘錄的重點。"],["elaborate","/ɪˈlæbəreɪt/","v.","詳細說明","Could you elaborate on your last job?","你可以詳細說明你上一份工作嗎？"],["unavailable","/ˌʌnəˈveɪləbəl/","adj.","沒空的；無法取得的","Mr. Lin is unavailable until three.","林先生三點前沒空。"],["tardiness","/ˈtɑːrdinəs/","n.","遲到","Tardiness affects your performance review.","遲到會影響你的績效考核。"],["proactive","/proʊˈæktɪv/","adj.","主動積極的","We value proactive employees who take initiative.","我們重視主動積極的員工。"],["adaptable","/əˈdæptəbəl/","adj.","適應力強的","The ideal candidate is adaptable and calm.","理想人選需適應力強且冷靜。"],["assertive","/əˈsɝːtɪv/","adj.","有自信的、果斷的","Managers need to be assertive but fair.","主管需要果斷但公正。"],["camaraderie","/ˌkɑːməˈrɑːdəri/","n.","同袍情誼","The retreat built camaraderie among staff.","員工旅遊增進了同事情誼。"],["retreat","/rɪˈtriːt/","n.","（公司）靜修會、員工旅遊","The annual staff retreat is in the mountains.","年度員工旅遊在山上舉行。"],["icebreaker","/ˈaɪsbreɪkər/","n.","破冰活動","We started the training with an icebreaker.","我們以破冰活動開啟培訓。"],["disgruntled","/dɪsˈgrʌntəld/","adj.","不滿的","A disgruntled employee complained to the union.","一位不滿的員工向工會投訴。"],["suspension","/səˈspenʃən/","n.","停職","She faces a two-week suspension without pay.","她面臨停職兩週且不支薪。"],["confidentiality agreement","/ˌkɑːnfɪˌdenʃiˈæləti əˌgriːmənt/","phr.","保密協議","New hires must sign a confidentiality agreement.","新進員工必須簽署保密協議。"],["adamant","/ˈædəmənt/","adj.","堅決的；堅持的","The director was adamant that the deadline would not change.","主任堅決表示截止日期不會變更。"],["adversely","/ædˈvɝsli/","adv.","不利地；負面地","The strike adversely affected our delivery schedule.","罷工對我們的交貨進度造成不利影響。"],["aggressively","/əˈɡrɛsɪvli/","adv.","積極地；強勢地","The company is aggressively expanding into overseas markets.","公司正積極拓展海外市場。"],["amply","/ˈæmpli/","adv.","充分地；大量地","Your efforts have been amply rewarded with a promotion.","你的努力已透過升遷獲得充分回報。"],["aptly","/ˈæptli/","adv.","恰當地；貼切地","The new product line is aptly named \"Easy Office.\"","新產品線取名「輕鬆辦公」，十分貼切。"],["arguably","/ˈɑrɡjuəbli/","adv.","可以說；按理說","This is arguably the best hotel in the city center.","這可以說是市中心最好的飯店。"],["aspiring","/əˈspaɪrɪŋ/","adj.","有抱負的；想成為…的","The workshop is designed for aspiring entrepreneurs.","這場工作坊專為有志創業者設計。"],["avid","/ˈævɪd/","adj.","熱衷的；渴望的","Our CEO is an avid reader of business books.","我們的執行長熱愛閱讀商業書籍。"],["bewildered","/bɪˈwɪldɚd/","adj.","困惑的；不知所措的","Some customers were bewildered by the new pricing system.","有些顧客對新的計價方式感到困惑。"],["by-product","/ˈbaɪˌprɑdʌkt/","n.","副產品；附帶結果","Heat is a by-product of the manufacturing process.","熱能是製造過程中的副產品。"],["candid","/ˈkændɪd/","adj.","坦率的；直言的","Thank you for your candid feedback on our proposal.","感謝您對我們提案的坦率回饋。"],["cease","/sis/","v.","停止；終止","The factory will cease operations at the end of the year.","該工廠將於年底停止營運。"],["coincide with","/ˌkoʊɪnˈsaɪd wɪð/","phr.","與…同時發生","The sale will coincide with the store's tenth anniversary.","這次特賣將與門市十週年同時舉行。"],["commendable","/kəˈmɛndəbəl/","adj.","值得稱讚的","The team showed commendable effort during the busy season.","團隊在旺季期間的努力值得嘉許。"],["commensurate","/kəˈmɛnsərət/","adj.","相稱的；相當的","Salary will be commensurate with experience.","薪資將依經驗而定。"],["condense","/kənˈdɛns/","v.","濃縮；精簡","Please condense the report into a one-page summary.","請把報告精簡成一頁的摘要。"],["confer","/kənˈfɝ/","v.","商議；授予","I need to confer with my partner before signing.","我簽約前需要先和合夥人商量。"],["conspicuous","/kənˈspɪkjuəs/","adj.","顯眼的；引人注目的","Place the safety sign in a conspicuous location.","請把安全標誌放在顯眼的位置。"],["contingent","/kənˈtɪndʒənt/","adj.","視…而定的（on）","The job offer is contingent on a background check.","這份錄取通知視背景調查結果而定。"],["correspondingly","/ˌkɔrəˈspɑndɪŋli/","adv.","相應地","Costs rose, and prices were raised correspondingly.","成本上升，價格也相應調漲。"],["defer","/dɪˈfɝ/","v.","延期；推遲","We decided to defer payment until next quarter.","我們決定將付款延到下一季。"],["definitive","/dɪˈfɪnətɪv/","adj.","最終的；權威性的","We expect a definitive answer from the client by Monday.","我們預計週一前會得到客戶的最終答覆。"],["devise","/dɪˈvaɪz/","v.","設計；想出（計畫）","Management devised a plan to reduce energy costs.","管理層想出了一套降低能源成本的計畫。"],["disperse","/dɪˈspɝs/","v.","分散；散開","The crowd began to disperse after the product launch.","產品發表會結束後，人潮開始散去。"],["embark on","/ɪmˈbɑrk ɑn/","phr.","著手；開始（新事業）","The company will embark on a major restructuring next year.","公司明年將著手進行大規模重整。"],["enact","/ɪˈnækt/","v.","制定（法律）；實施","The government enacted new rules on product labeling.","政府制定了產品標示的新規定。"],["exemplary","/ɪɡˈzɛmpləri/","adj.","模範的；堪為楷模的","She was praised for her exemplary customer service.","她因模範級的客戶服務而受到表揚。"],["exquisite","/ɪkˈskwɪzɪt/","adj.","精緻的；精美的","The restaurant is famous for its exquisite desserts.","這家餐廳以精緻甜點聞名。"],["inaugural","/ɪˈnɔɡjərəl/","adj.","首次的；就職的","The inaugural flight to Osaka departs next month.","飛往大阪的首航班機下個月起飛。"],["incrementally","/ˌɪŋkrəˈmɛntəli/","adv.","逐步地；遞增地","Prices will be raised incrementally over two years.","價格將在兩年內逐步調漲。"],["inevitably","/ɪnˈɛvɪtəbli/","adv.","不可避免地","Rising fuel costs will inevitably affect airfares.","燃料成本上漲將無可避免地影響機票價格。"],["influx","/ˈɪnˌflʌks/","n.","湧入；大量流入","Hotels expect an influx of tourists during the festival.","飯店預期節慶期間會有大批遊客湧入。"],["intermittent","/ˌɪntɚˈmɪtənt/","adj.","間歇的；斷斷續續的","Intermittent rain is expected throughout the weekend.","整個週末預計會有間歇性降雨。"],["irreplaceable","/ˌɪrɪˈpleɪsəbəl/","adj.","無法取代的","Her experience makes her irreplaceable to the team.","她的經驗使她在團隊中無可取代。"],["jeopardize","/ˈdʒɛpɚˌdaɪz/","v.","危及；使陷入危險","Late deliveries could jeopardize our contract with the client.","延遲交貨可能危及我們和客戶的合約。"],["lavish","/ˈlævɪʃ/","adj.","奢華的；豐盛的","The company held a lavish dinner for its top clients.","公司為頂級客戶舉辦了一場奢華晚宴。"],["optimal","/ˈɑptəməl/","adj.","最佳的；最理想的","Store the product at room temperature for optimal results.","將產品置於室溫保存以獲得最佳效果。"],["premier","/prɪˈmɪr/","adj.","首要的；頂尖的","We are the premier supplier of office furniture in the region.","我們是該地區頂尖的辦公家具供應商。"],["prevail","/prɪˈveɪl/","v.","盛行；占上風","Dry conditions will prevail for the rest of the week.","本週接下來都將是乾燥的天氣。"],["prosper","/ˈprɑspɚ/","v.","繁榮；興旺","Small businesses prosper when the local economy grows.","地方經濟成長時，小型企業就會興旺。"],["seamlessly","/ˈsimləsli/","adv.","順暢地；無縫地","The new software works seamlessly with our existing system.","新軟體能與我們現有的系統無縫整合。"],["signify","/ˈsɪɡnəˌfaɪ/","v.","表示；意味著","A green light signifies that the machine is ready.","綠燈表示機器已準備就緒。"],["sophisticated","/səˈfɪstəˌkeɪtɪd/","adj.","精密的；高階的；老練的","The warehouse uses a sophisticated tracking system.","倉庫使用一套精密的追蹤系統。"],["sparingly","/ˈspɛrɪŋli/","adv.","節約地；少量地","Please use office supplies sparingly to reduce costs.","請節約使用辦公用品以降低成本。"],["tremendous","/trɪˈmɛndəs/","adj.","巨大的；極好的","The new product has been a tremendous success.","新產品大獲成功。"],["underway","/ˌʌndɚˈweɪ/","adj.","進行中的","Construction of the new plant is already underway.","新廠房的興建工程已經在進行中。"],["vigorously","/ˈvɪɡərəsli/","adv.","大力地；積極地","The company is vigorously promoting its new service.","公司正大力推廣其新服務。"],["wholeheartedly","/ˌhoʊlˈhɑrtɪdli/","adv.","全心全意地","We wholeheartedly support the new recycling policy.","我們全心支持新的回收政策。"],["accreditation","/əˌkrɛdəˈteɪʃən/","n.","認證；鑑定合格","The lab received accreditation from the national agency.","該實驗室獲得國家機構的認證。"],["abundance","/əˈbʌndəns/","n.","豐富；大量","The region has an abundance of skilled workers.","該地區擁有大量技術純熟的工人。"],["aftermath","/ˈæftɚˌmæθ/","n.","（災難等的）後果；餘波","In the aftermath of the storm, many flights were canceled.","暴風雨過後，許多航班被取消。"],["appointee","/əˌpɔɪnˈti/","n.","被任命者","The new appointee will lead the finance department.","新任命的人員將領導財務部。"],["upholstery","/əpˈhoʊlstəri/","n.","（家具的）布套；軟墊","The upholstery on the lobby sofas will be replaced.","大廳沙發的布套將會更換。"],["be advised that","/bi ədˈvaɪzd ðæt/","phr.","請注意；特此通知","Please be advised that the office will close early on Friday.","特此通知，辦公室週五將提早關閉。"],["at one's disposal","/æt wʌnz dɪˈspoʊzəl/","phr.","任由某人使用；供某人支配","A company car will be at your disposal during the visit.","拜訪期間會有一輛公務車供您使用。"],["in an effort to","/ɪn ən ˈɛfɚt tu/","phr.","為了；努力想要","In an effort to cut costs, we switched suppliers.","為了降低成本，我們更換了供應商。"],["meet a demand","/mit ə dɪˈmænd/","phr.","滿足需求","We added a night shift to meet a demand for more units.","我們增設夜班以滿足增加產量的需求。"],["meet expectations","/mit ˌɛkspɛkˈteɪʃənz/","phr.","符合期望","The quarterly results did not meet expectations.","季度業績未達預期。"],["launch a product","/lɔntʃ ə ˈprɑdʌkt/","phr.","推出產品","We plan to launch a product for the Japanese market.","我們計畫推出一款針對日本市場的產品。"],["go out of business","/ɡoʊ aʊt əv ˈbɪznəs/","phr.","倒閉；歇業","Several local shops went out of business last year.","去年好幾家當地商店歇業了。"],["review an application","/rɪˈvju ən ˌæpləˈkeɪʃən/","phr.","審核申請","It takes two weeks to review an application for a loan.","審核一份貸款申請需要兩週。"],["exceed the budget","/ɪkˈsid ðə ˈbʌdʒɪt/","phr.","超出預算","The renovation project may exceed the budget by ten percent.","這項整修工程可能超出預算百分之十。"],["approve a budget","/əˈpruv ə ˈbʌdʒɪt/","phr.","批准預算","The board will approve a budget for next year in November.","董事會將在十一月批准明年的預算。"],["performance evaluation","/pɚˈfɔrməns ɪˌvæljuˈeɪʃən/","n.","績效評估","Your performance evaluation is scheduled for next Monday.","你的績效評估安排在下週一。"],["sales volume","/seɪlz ˈvɑljum/","n.","銷售量","Sales volume dropped slightly due to the price increase.","由於漲價，銷售量略為下滑。"],["sales quota","/seɪlz ˈkwoʊtə/","n.","業績配額","Each representative must reach a monthly sales quota.","每位業務代表都必須達成每月業績配額。"],["safety manual","/ˈseɪfti ˈmænjuəl/","n.","安全手冊","All machine operators must read the safety manual.","所有機台操作員都必須閱讀安全手冊。"],["job requirements","/dʒɑb rɪˈkwaɪrmənts/","n.","職務要求","Please read the job requirements carefully before applying.","申請前請仔細閱讀職務要求。"],["limited time offer","/ˈlɪmɪtɪd taɪm ˈɔfɚ/","n.","限時優惠","This limited time offer ends on Sunday.","這項限時優惠將於週日結束。"],["accrued","/əˈkruːd/","adj.","累計的；應計的","Accrued interest is added to the account each month.","應計利息每月計入帳戶。"],["accrual","/əˈkruːəl/","n.","應計；累積","Vacation accruals are recorded as a liability.","特休的應計額以負債入帳。"],["accounts payable","/əˌkaʊnts ˈpeɪəbəl/","phr.","應付帳款；應付帳款部門","Send supplier invoices to accounts payable.","請將供應商發票交給應付帳款部門。"],["accounts receivable","/əˌkaʊnts rɪˈsiːvəbəl/","phr.","應收帳款","Accounts receivable rose because clients paid late.","因客戶延遲付款，應收帳款增加。"],["amortization","/ˌæmərtəˈzeɪʃən/","n.","攤銷；分期償還","The amortization schedule shows each monthly payment.","攤還表列出每月的付款金額。"],["depreciate","/dɪˈpriːʃieɪt/","v.","折舊；貶值","Company cars depreciate quickly.","公司車輛折舊得很快。"],["appreciation","/əˌpriːʃiˈeɪʃən/","n.","增值；升值","The appreciation of the yen hurt Japanese exporters.","日圓升值打擊了日本出口商。"],["liabilities","/ˌlaɪəˈbɪlətiz/","n.","負債","Total liabilities fell by ten percent.","總負債減少了百分之十。"],["venture capital","/ˌventʃər ˈkæpɪtəl/","phr.","創投資金","The startup raised money from venture capital firms.","這家新創公司向創投公司募得資金。"],["working capital","/ˌwɝːkɪŋ ˈkæpɪtəl/","phr.","營運資金","We need more working capital to fill large orders.","我們需要更多營運資金來應付大訂單。"],["capital investment","/ˌkæpɪtəl ɪnˈvestmənt/","phr.","資本投資","The plant requires a major capital investment.","這座工廠需要大筆資本投資。"],["profit and loss","/ˌprɑːfɪt ən ˈlɔːs/","phr.","損益","The profit and loss statement is updated monthly.","損益表每月更新。"],["outlay","/ˈaʊtleɪ/","n.","支出；開銷","The initial outlay for the system is high.","這套系統的初期支出很高。"],["deductible","/dɪˈdʌktəbəl/","adj./n.","可扣除的；（保險）自付額","Office supplies are deductible business expenses.","辦公用品屬可扣除的營業費用。"],["customs duty","/ˈkʌstəmz ˌduːti/","phr.","關稅","Customs duty is charged on imported goods.","進口商品須課徵關稅。"],["VAT","/ˌviː eɪ ˈtiː/","n.","加值型營業稅","All prices include twenty percent VAT.","所有價格均含百分之二十的加值稅。"],["withholding","/wɪðˈhoʊldɪŋ/","n.","預扣（稅款）","Check the withholding on your pay stub.","請核對薪資明細上的預扣稅款。"],["external audit","/ɪkˌstɝːnəl ˈɔːdɪt/","phr.","外部審計","An external audit is required by law.","法律規定必須進行外部審計。"],["general ledger","/ˌdʒenərəl ˈledʒər/","phr.","總分類帳","All transactions are posted to the general ledger.","所有交易都過帳到總分類帳。"],["journal entry","/ˈdʒɝːnəl ˌentri/","phr.","日記帳分錄","The accountant made a journal entry for the refund.","會計為這筆退款做了一筆分錄。"],["reconciliation","/ˌrekənˌsɪliˈeɪʃən/","n.","對帳；調節","Bank reconciliation is done at the end of each month.","每月底進行銀行對帳。"],["inaccuracy","/ɪnˈækjərəsi/","n.","不正確；錯誤之處","The auditor found several inaccuracies in the report.","稽核員在報告中發現幾處錯誤。"],["verification","/ˌverɪfɪˈkeɪʃən/","n.","核實；驗證","Large transfers require additional verification.","大額轉帳需要額外驗證。"],["fraudulent","/ˈfrɔːdʒələnt/","adj.","詐欺的；舞弊的","The bank blocked several fraudulent transactions.","銀行攔下了數筆詐欺交易。"],["embezzle","/ɪmˈbezəl/","v.","侵占；盜用（公款）","The clerk was accused of embezzling company funds.","那名職員被控侵占公司資金。"],["embezzlement","/ɪmˈbezəlmənt/","n.","侵占；盜用公款","The audit uncovered a case of embezzlement.","稽核發現一起侵占公款案件。"],["diversification","/dəˌvɝːsɪfɪˈkeɪʃən/","n.","多角化；分散投資","Diversification reduces investment risk.","分散投資可降低風險。"],["securities","/sɪˈkjʊrətiz/","n.","有價證券","The bank trades stocks, bonds, and other securities.","這家銀行買賣股票、債券和其他有價證券。"],["initial public offering","/ɪˌnɪʃəl ˌpʌblɪk ˈɔːfərɪŋ/","phr.","首次公開發行（IPO）","The initial public offering raised $200 million.","首次公開發行募得兩億美元。"],["skyrocket","/ˈskaɪˌrɑːkɪt/","v.","飆升；暴漲","Fuel costs skyrocketed last summer.","去年夏天燃料成本暴漲。"],["deflation","/dɪˈfleɪʃən/","n.","通貨緊縮","Deflation can make consumers delay purchases.","通貨緊縮可能讓消費者延後購買。"],["compound interest","/ˌkɑːmpaʊnd ˈɪntrəst/","phr.","複利","Compound interest helps savings grow faster.","複利讓存款增加得更快。"],["approve a loan","/əˌpruːv ə ˈloʊn/","phr.","核准貸款","The bank approved a loan for the expansion.","銀行核准了擴廠貸款。"],["credit line","/ˈkredɪt ˌlaɪn/","phr.","信用額度","We drew on our credit line to pay suppliers.","我們動用信用額度支付供應商。"],["creditworthy","/ˈkredɪtˌwɝːði/","adj.","信用良好的；有償債能力的","Banks lend only to creditworthy customers.","銀行只貸款給信用良好的客戶。"],["debtor","/ˈdetər/","n.","債務人","The debtor agreed to a new payment plan.","債務人同意新的還款計畫。"],["liquidate","/ˈlɪkwɪdeɪt/","v.","清算；變賣（資產）","The firm had to liquidate its assets.","這家公司被迫清算資產。"],["liquidation","/ˌlɪkwɪˈdeɪʃən/","n.","清算；清盤","The retailer went into liquidation last month.","那家零售商上個月進入清算程序。"],["debt collection","/ˈdet kəˌlekʃən/","phr.","催收債務","Overdue accounts are sent to debt collection.","逾期帳款會轉交催收。"],["bounced check","/ˌbaʊnst ˈtʃek/","phr.","空頭支票；跳票","The bank charges a fee for a bounced check.","銀行對跳票收取手續費。"],["statement of account","/ˌsteɪtmənt əv əˈkaʊnt/","phr.","對帳單；帳戶結單","We send each client a monthly statement of account.","我們每月寄對帳單給每位客戶。"],["bill to","/ˈbɪl ˌtuː/","phr.","帳單寄送給；向……開帳","Please bill the repairs to our main office.","請將維修費用開帳給我們總公司。"],["pro forma invoice","/proʊ ˌfɔːrmə ˈɪnvɔɪs/","phr.","形式發票；預估發票","The buyer asked for a pro forma invoice first.","買方要求先提供形式發票。"],["beneficiary","/ˌbenɪˈfɪʃieri/","n.","受益人；收款人","Enter the beneficiary's bank details.","請輸入收款人的銀行資料。"],["prepay","/ˌpriːˈpeɪ/","v.","預付","Guests must prepay for the first night.","房客須預付第一晚的房費。"],["buy on credit","/ˌbaɪ ɑːn ˈkredɪt/","phr.","賒購","Many firms buy materials on credit.","許多公司以賒購方式購買原料。"],["arrears","/əˈrɪrz/","n.","欠款；拖欠款項","The tenant is two months in arrears.","那位房客已拖欠兩個月的租金。"],["credit note","/ˈkredɪt ˌnoʊt/","phr.","折讓單；貸項通知單","We issued a credit note for the damaged goods.","我們針對損壞的貨品開立了折讓單。"],["treasury","/ˈtreʒəri/","n.","財政部；（公司）資金部","The treasury department manages the company's cash.","資金部負責管理公司的現金。"],["controller","/kənˈtroʊlər/","n.","會計主管；財務長","The controller reviews all monthly reports.","會計主管審核所有月報。"],["cost-efficient","/ˌkɔːst ɪˈfɪʃənt/","adj.","具成本效率的","LED lights are more cost-efficient.","LED 燈較具成本效益。"],["cost-cutting","/ˈkɔːst ˌkʌtɪŋ/","adj./n.","削減成本的；成本削減","The cost-cutting plan saved two million dollars.","削減成本計畫省下了兩百萬美元。"],["budget deficit","/ˈbʌdʒɪt ˌdefɪsɪt/","phr.","預算赤字","The city faces a large budget deficit.","該市面臨龐大的預算赤字。"],["budget surplus","/ˈbʌdʒɪt ˌsɝːpləs/","phr.","預算盈餘","The budget surplus will fund new parks.","預算盈餘將用於興建新公園。"],["allocate funds","/ˌæləkeɪt ˈfʌndz/","phr.","分配資金","The board will allocate funds for research.","董事會將撥款給研發。"],["earmark","/ˈɪrmɑːrk/","v.","指定（用途）；專款撥用","The money is earmarked for new equipment.","這筆錢指定用於購買新設備。"],["subsidize","/ˈsʌbsɪdaɪz/","v.","補貼；資助","The company subsidizes employee lunches.","公司補貼員工午餐。"],["expend","/ɪkˈspend/","v.","花費；耗費","Too much effort was expended on the old system.","在舊系統上耗費了太多心力。"],["squander","/ˈskwɑːndər/","v.","浪費；揮霍","He squandered the budget on unnecessary trips.","他把預算浪費在不必要的出差上。"],["austerity","/ɔːˈsterəti/","n.","撙節；緊縮","The government announced new austerity measures.","政府宣布了新的撙節措施。"],["budgetary","/ˈbʌdʒɪteri/","adj.","預算的","We face strict budgetary limits this year.","我們今年面臨嚴格的預算限制。"],["priceless","/ˈpraɪsləs/","adj.","無價的；極珍貴的","Customer trust is priceless.","顧客的信任是無價的。"],["fiscal policy","/ˌfɪskəl ˈpɑːləsi/","phr.","財政政策","The new fiscal policy cuts taxes for families.","新財政政策為家庭減稅。"],["monetary policy","/ˌmɑːnəteri ˈpɑːləsi/","phr.","貨幣政策","Monetary policy affects interest rates.","貨幣政策會影響利率。"],["gross domestic product","/ˌɡroʊs dəˌmestɪk ˈprɑːdʌkt/","phr.","國內生產毛額","Gross domestic product rose for the third quarter.","國內生產毛額連續第三季成長。"],["macroeconomic","/ˌmækroʊˌekəˈnɑːmɪk/","adj.","總體經濟的","The report analyzes macroeconomic trends.","這份報告分析總體經濟趨勢。"],["consumer price index","/kənˌsuːmər ˈpraɪs ˌɪndeks/","phr.","消費者物價指數","The consumer price index rose two percent.","消費者物價指數上升百分之二。"],["trade deficit","/ˈtreɪd ˌdefɪsɪt/","phr.","貿易逆差","The trade deficit widened last month.","上個月貿易逆差擴大。"],["trade surplus","/ˈtreɪd ˌsɝːpləs/","phr.","貿易順差","The country reported a record trade surplus.","該國公布創紀錄的貿易順差。"],["balance of trade","/ˌbæləns əv ˈtreɪd/","phr.","貿易收支","Exports improved the balance of trade.","出口改善了貿易收支。"],["asset management","/ˈæset ˌmænɪdʒmənt/","phr.","資產管理","She works for an asset management firm.","她在一家資產管理公司工作。"],["wealth management","/ˈwelθ ˌmænɪdʒmənt/","phr.","財富管理","The bank expanded its wealth management services.","這家銀行擴大了財富管理服務。"],["annuity","/əˈnuːəti/","n.","年金","He receives an annuity every year.","他每年領取一筆年金。"],["interest-bearing","/ˈɪntrəst ˌberɪŋ/","adj.","生息的；附利息的","Keep extra cash in an interest-bearing account.","把多餘的現金存在生息帳戶。"],["certificate of deposit","/sərˌtɪfɪkət əv dɪˈpɑːzɪt/","phr.","定期存單","A certificate of deposit pays a fixed rate.","定期存單提供固定利率。"],["index fund","/ˈɪndeks ˌfʌnd/","phr.","指數型基金","Index funds have very low fees.","指數型基金的費用很低。"],["hedge fund","/ˈhedʒ ˌfʌnd/","phr.","避險基金；對沖基金","The hedge fund made large profits last year.","這檔避險基金去年獲利豐厚。"],["capital gains","/ˌkæpɪtəl ˈɡeɪnz/","phr.","資本利得","Capital gains from stock sales are taxable.","出售股票的資本利得須課稅。"],["capital gains tax","/ˌkæpɪtəl ˈɡeɪnz ˌtæks/","phr.","資本利得稅","You may owe capital gains tax on the sale.","這筆出售可能須繳資本利得稅。"],["tax bracket","/ˈtæks ˌbrækɪt/","phr.","稅級；課稅級距","His raise moved him into a higher tax bracket.","加薪讓他進入更高的稅級。"],["tax audit","/ˈtæks ˌɔːdɪt/","phr.","稅務稽查","Keep receipts in case of a tax audit.","請保留收據以備稅務稽查。"],["tax evasion","/ˈtæks ɪˌveɪʒən/","phr.","逃稅","The owner was charged with tax evasion.","老闆被控逃稅。"],["close the books","/ˌkloʊz ðə ˈbʊks/","phr.","結帳；關帳","We close the books on the fifth of each month.","我們每月五日關帳。"],["cook the books","/ˌkʊk ðə ˈbʊks/","phr.","做假帳","The manager was fired for cooking the books.","經理因做假帳被開除。"],["co-sign","/ˌkoʊ ˈsaɪn/","v.","共同簽署；擔保","Her father co-signed the loan.","她父親替那筆貸款作保。"],["dividend income","/ˈdɪvɪdend ˌɪnkʌm/","phr.","股利收入","Dividend income makes up part of her earnings.","股利收入是她收入的一部分。"],["operating income","/ˈɑːpəreɪtɪŋ ˌɪnkʌm/","phr.","營業收入；營業利益","Operating income improved despite lower sales.","儘管銷售下滑，營業利益仍有改善。"],["gross margin","/ˌɡroʊs ˈmɑːrdʒɪn/","phr.","毛利率","Our gross margin is about forty percent.","我們的毛利率約為百分之四十。"],["net margin","/ˌnet ˈmɑːrdʒɪn/","phr.","淨利率","The net margin shrank because of higher taxes.","因稅負增加，淨利率縮小。"],["earnings per share","/ˌɝːnɪŋz pər ˈʃer/","phr.","每股盈餘","Earnings per share rose to two dollars.","每股盈餘升至兩美元。"],["debt-to-equity ratio","/ˌdet tuː ˈekwəti ˌreɪʃioʊ/","phr.","負債權益比","A low debt-to-equity ratio reassures lenders.","低負債權益比讓放款機構安心。"],["leveraged","/ˈlevərɪdʒd/","adj.","槓桿的；舉債經營的","The deal was a leveraged buyout.","這筆交易是槓桿收購。"],["solvent","/ˈsɑːlvənt/","adj.","有償債能力的","The bank remained solvent during the crisis.","這家銀行在危機期間仍有償債能力。"],["current assets","/ˌkɝːənt ˈæsets/","phr.","流動資產","Current assets include cash and inventory.","流動資產包含現金和存貨。"],["intangible assets","/ɪnˌtændʒəbəl ˈæsets/","phr.","無形資產","Patents and brands are intangible assets.","專利和品牌屬於無形資產。"],["goodwill","/ˌɡʊdˈwɪl/","n.","商譽","The purchase price included goodwill.","收購價格包含了商譽。"],["write-off","/ˈraɪt ˌɔːf/","n.","沖銷；註銷；可抵稅支出","The bad loan was recorded as a write-off.","這筆呆帳被列為沖銷。"],["write down","/ˌraɪt ˈdaʊn/","phr.","降低帳面價值；減記","The firm wrote down the value of its old stock.","公司下調了舊存貨的帳面價值。"],["provision","/prəˈvɪʒən/","n.","準備；提撥；條款","We made a provision for possible losses.","我們為可能的損失提列了準備。"],["contingency fund","/kənˈtɪndʒənsi ˌfʌnd/","phr.","應變基金；備用金","Unexpected repairs were paid from the contingency fund.","突發維修費用由備用金支付。"],["nest egg","/ˈnest ˌeɡ/","phr.","儲備金；養老金","They built a nice nest egg for retirement.","他們為退休存了一筆可觀的積蓄。"],["household income","/ˌhaʊshoʊld ˈɪnkʌm/","phr.","家庭收入","Average household income rose this year.","今年平均家庭收入上升。"],["restructuring","/riːˈstrʌktʃərɪŋ/","n.","重組；改組","The restructuring saved the company from bankruptcy.","重組讓公司免於破產。"],["cost overrun","/ˈkɔːst ˌoʊvərʌn/","phr.","成本超支","Cost overruns delayed the new terminal.","成本超支延誤了新航廈的工程。"],["underspend","/ˌʌndərˈspend/","v.","未用完（預算）；少花","We underspent our travel budget this year.","我們今年的差旅預算沒用完。"],["budget constraints","/ˈbʌdʒɪt kənˌstreɪnts/","phr.","預算限制","Due to budget constraints, hiring is on hold.","因預算限制，招聘暫停。"],["financial stability","/faɪˌnænʃəl stəˈbɪləti/","phr.","財務穩定","The merger will improve our financial stability.","這次合併將提升我們的財務穩定性。"],["fiscally responsible","/ˌfɪskəli rɪˈspɑːnsəbəl/","phr.","財務負責的；量入為出的","The mayor promised to be fiscally responsible.","市長承諾會審慎理財。"],["earnings call","/ˈɝːnɪŋz ˌkɔːl/","phr.","法說會；財報電話會議","The CEO answered questions during the earnings call.","執行長在法說會上回答問題。"],["profit warning","/ˈprɑːfɪt ˌwɔːrnɪŋ/","phr.","獲利預警","Shares fell after the profit warning.","發布獲利預警後股價下跌。"],["refinance","/ˌriːˈfaɪnæns/","v.","再融資；轉貸","They refinanced the mortgage at a lower rate.","他們以較低利率轉貸房貸。"],["repayment schedule","/rɪˈpeɪmənt ˌskedʒuːl/","phr.","還款計畫表","The repayment schedule runs for five years.","還款計畫為期五年。"],["loan term","/ˈloʊn ˌtɝːm/","phr.","貸款期限","A longer loan term means lower monthly payments.","貸款期限越長，每月還款越低。"],["annual percentage rate","/ˌænjuəl pərˈsentɪdʒ ˌreɪt/","phr.","年利率；年百分率","Compare the annual percentage rate before you borrow.","借款前請比較年利率。"],["APR","/ˌeɪ piː ˈɑːr/","n.","年利率","The card has an APR of eighteen percent.","這張卡的年利率是百分之十八。"],["lump-sum payment","/ˌlʌmp sʌm ˈpeɪmənt/","phr.","一次付清","We offer a discount for a lump-sum payment.","一次付清可享折扣。"],["book value","/ˈbʊk ˌvæljuː/","phr.","帳面價值","The shares trade below book value.","這檔股票的股價低於帳面價值。"],["face value","/ˈfeɪs ˌvæljuː/","phr.","面值；票面價值","The bond will be repaid at face value.","這張債券將按面值償還。"],["appraised value","/əˌpreɪzd ˈvæljuː/","phr.","估定價值","The appraised value of the land was higher than expected.","土地的估定價值比預期高。"],["fair market value","/ˌfer ˌmɑːrkɪt ˈvæljuː/","phr.","公允市價","The shares were sold at fair market value.","這些股票以公允市價出售。"],["financier","/ˌfɪnənˈsɪr/","n.","金融家；投資者","A wealthy financier backed the project.","一位富有的金融家資助這個計畫。"],["capitalization","/ˌkæpɪtələˈzeɪʃən/","n.","資本總額；市值","The company has a market capitalization of $5 billion.","這家公司市值五十億美元。"],["regulator","/ˈreɡjəleɪtər/","n.","監管機構","Financial regulators fined the bank heavily.","金融監管機構重罰了這家銀行。"],["irregularity","/ɪˌreɡjəˈlærəti/","n.","不合規之處；異常","The audit revealed some accounting irregularities.","稽核發現一些會計異常。"],["miscalculation","/ˌmɪskælkjəˈleɪʃən/","n.","計算錯誤；誤判","A miscalculation led to the budget shortfall.","一個計算錯誤導致預算短缺。"],["underestimate","/ˌʌndərˈestɪmeɪt/","v.","低估","We underestimated the cost of shipping.","我們低估了運費。"],["overestimate","/ˌoʊvərˈestɪmeɪt/","v.","高估","Analysts overestimated demand for the product.","分析師高估了該產品的需求。"],["tally","/ˈtæli/","v./n.","計算；總計；記錄","Please tally the receipts from the trip.","請把這趟出差的收據加總。"],["itemization","/ˌaɪtəməˈzeɪʃən/","n.","逐項列舉；明細","The client requested an itemization of all charges.","客戶要求列出所有費用的明細。"],["royalties","/ˈrɔɪəltiz/","n.","權利金；版稅","The author earns royalties on every copy sold.","作者每賣出一本書就能領版稅。"],["gratuity","/ɡrəˈtuːəti/","n.","小費；賞金","A fifteen percent gratuity is included.","已含百分之十五的小費。"],["profit-sharing","/ˈprɑːfɪt ˌʃerɪŋ/","n.","分紅制度；利潤分享","Employees join the profit-sharing plan after a year.","員工任職一年後可加入分紅計畫。"],["foot the bill","/ˌfʊt ðə ˈbɪl/","phr.","付帳；負擔費用","The company will foot the bill for the conference.","公司將負擔研討會的費用。"],["pick up the tab","/ˌpɪk ʌp ðə ˈtæb/","phr.","買單；付帳","Our client picked up the tab for dinner.","我們的客戶請了晚餐。"],["devaluation","/diːˌvæljuˈeɪʃən/","n.","（貨幣）貶值","The devaluation made imports more expensive.","貨幣貶值使進口品變貴。"],["escrow","/ˈeskroʊ/","n.","第三方託管；履約保證","The deposit is held in escrow until closing.","訂金由第三方託管至交割為止。"],["upswing","/ˈʌpswɪŋ/","n.","好轉；上升趨勢","The market is on an upswing.","市場正處於上升趨勢。"],["bottom out","/ˌbɑːtəm ˈaʊt/","phr.","觸底","Housing prices appear to have bottomed out.","房價似乎已經觸底。"],["bull market","/ˈbʊl ˌmɑːrkɪt/","phr.","多頭市場；牛市","Investors made money during the bull market.","投資人在多頭市場中賺了錢。"],["bear market","/ˈber ˌmɑːrkɪt/","phr.","空頭市場；熊市","Many funds lost value in the bear market.","許多基金在空頭市場中縮水。"],["hit a record high","/ˌhɪt ə ˌrekərd ˈhaɪ/","phr.","創新高","The index hit a record high on Monday.","該指數週一創下歷史新高。"],["blockbuster","/ˈblɑːkbʌstər/","n./adj.","暢銷大作；極成功的","The new game became a blockbuster in its first week.","這款新遊戲第一週就成為熱賣大作。"],["conversion","/kənˈvɜːrʒn/","n.","轉換（率）；轉變","We want to improve the conversion of visitors into buyers.","我們想提高訪客轉換成買家的比率。"],["dominant","/ˈdɑːmɪnənt/","adj.","主導的、占優勢的","The firm holds a dominant position in the market.","這家公司在市場上居主導地位。"],["gauge","/ɡeɪdʒ/","v./n.","評估、測量；標準","We used a survey to gauge customer interest.","我們用調查來評估顧客的興趣。"],["gimmick","/ˈɡɪmɪk/","n.","噱頭、花招","The free gift was just a marketing gimmick.","那份免費禮物只是行銷噱頭。"],["impulse","/ˈɪmpʌls/","n.","衝動","Many shoppers buy snacks on impulse.","很多購物者會衝動購買零食。"],["introductory","/ˌɪntrəˈdʌktəri/","adj.","介紹的、首次推出的","The introductory price is valid until May.","首發價格到五月為止有效。"],["jingle","/ˈdʒɪŋɡl/","n.","廣告歌曲","Everyone remembers the jingle from that TV ad.","大家都記得那支電視廣告的廣告歌。"],["lasting","/ˈlæstɪŋ/","adj.","持久的","We want to leave a lasting impression on customers.","我們想在顧客心中留下持久的印象。"],["lead","/liːd/","n.","潛在客戶名單、銷售線索","The trade show gave us over 200 new leads.","這次商展帶給我們兩百多筆新的銷售線索。"],["line","/laɪn/","n.","產品系列、商品線","The designer launched a new line of handbags.","設計師推出了新的手提包系列。"],["mainstream","/ˈmeɪnstriːm/","adj./n.","主流的；主流","Electric cars are becoming mainstream.","電動車正成為主流。"],["markdown","/ˈmɑːrkdaʊn/","n.","降價、減價","Look for markdowns on the back shelves.","請到後面的貨架找降價商品。"],["marketable","/ˈmɑːrkɪtəbl/","adj.","有市場的、好賣的","The idea is creative but not very marketable.","這個點子有創意，但不太有市場。"],["mass-produce","/ˌmæs prəˈduːs/","v.","大量生產","We plan to mass-produce the toy next year.","我們計畫明年大量生產這款玩具。"],["merchandising","/ˈmɜːrtʃəndaɪzɪŋ/","n.","商品企劃與陳列；周邊商品","Good merchandising can increase sales in a small store.","好的商品陳列能提高小店的銷售。"],["novelty","/ˈnɑːvlti/","n.","新奇（的事物）；小玩意","The novelty of the product wore off quickly.","這項產品的新鮮感很快就退了。"],["overprice","/ˌoʊvərˈpraɪs/","v.","定價過高","If we overprice the product, it won't sell.","如果我們定價過高，產品會賣不出去。"],["perception","/pərˈsepʃn/","n.","看法、認知","We need to change the public perception of our brand.","我們需要改變大眾對我們品牌的看法。"],["point of sale","/ˌpɔɪnt əv ˈseɪl/","phr.","銷售點、收銀端","Point-of-sale displays encourage last-minute purchases.","收銀台旁的陳列能促成臨時購買。"],["prestigious","/preˈstɪdʒəs/","adj.","有聲望的、聲譽卓著的","The brand won a prestigious design award.","這個品牌獲得了一項極具聲望的設計獎。"],["prospect","/ˈprɑːspekt/","n.","潛在客戶；前景","She called every prospect on the list.","她打給名單上的每一位潛在客戶。"],["receptive","/rɪˈseptɪv/","adj.","願意接受的、反應良好的","Consumers were receptive to the new flavor.","消費者對新口味反應良好。"],["saturate","/ˈsætʃəreɪt/","v.","使飽和","Cheap phones have saturated the market.","廉價手機已使市場飽和。"],["shoplifting","/ˈʃɑːplɪftɪŋ/","n.","順手牽羊、商店竊盜","Security cameras help prevent shoplifting.","監視器有助於防止商店竊盜。"],["statistics","/stəˈtɪstɪks/","n.","統計數據；統計學","The statistics show a rise in online sales.","統計數據顯示網路銷售上升。"],["tactic","/ˈtæktɪk/","n.","策略、手法","Free trials are a common sales tactic.","免費試用是常見的銷售手法。"],["tagline","/ˈtæɡlaɪn/","n.","廣告標語、品牌口號","The tagline appears at the end of every commercial.","品牌口號出現在每支廣告的結尾。"],["telemarketing","/ˌtelɪˈmɑːrkɪtɪŋ/","n.","電話行銷","Many people dislike telemarketing calls at dinnertime.","許多人討厭晚餐時間的電話行銷。"],["undercut","/ˌʌndərˈkʌt/","v.","削價競爭、以更低價搶客","The new store undercut our prices by 10 percent.","新開的店比我們便宜一成搶客。"],["upscale","/ˌʌpˈskeɪl/","adj.","高檔的、高級的","The mall attracts upscale shoppers.","這間購物中心吸引高消費族群。"],["acclaim","/əˈkleɪm/","n./v.","讚譽；稱讚","The product received wide acclaim from reviewers.","這項產品獲得評論者廣泛讚譽。"],["adopt","/əˈdɑːpt/","v.","採用","More stores are adopting mobile payment.","愈來愈多商店採用行動支付。"],["big-ticket","/ˌbɪɡ ˈtɪkɪt/","adj.","高價的、昂貴的","Customers delay big-ticket purchases during a downturn.","景氣不佳時，顧客會延後購買高價商品。"],["buyer's remorse","/ˌbaɪərz rɪˈmɔːrs/","phr.","買後後悔","A generous return policy reduces buyer's remorse.","寬鬆的退貨政策能減少買後後悔。"],["consumer behavior","/kənˌsuːmər bɪˈheɪvjər/","phr.","消費者行為","The study looks at consumer behavior online.","這項研究探討網路上的消費者行為。"],["cross-sell","/ˌkrɔːs ˈsel/","v.","交叉銷售","Staff are trained to cross-sell related products.","員工受過訓練，會交叉銷售相關產品。"],["customer loyalty","/ˌkʌstəmər ˈlɔɪəlti/","phr.","顧客忠誠度","Reward points help build customer loyalty.","紅利點數有助於建立顧客忠誠度。"],["customer retention","/ˌkʌstəmər rɪˈtenʃn/","phr.","顧客留存（率）","Customer retention is cheaper than finding new clients.","留住顧客比開發新客戶便宜。"],["depict","/dɪˈpɪkt/","v.","描繪、描述","The ad depicts a happy family using the car.","這則廣告描繪一個幸福家庭使用這輛車。"],["discerning","/dɪˈsɜːrnɪŋ/","adj.","有眼光的、識貨的","Our wines are chosen for discerning customers.","我們的葡萄酒是為識貨的顧客挑選的。"],["first-hand","/ˌfɜːrst ˈhænd/","adj./adv.","第一手的；直接地","Visit the showroom to see the quality first-hand.","請親臨展示間直接看看品質。"],["flagship","/ˈflæɡʃɪp/","n./adj.","旗艦（產品、店）；最重要的","The phone is the company's flagship product.","這支手機是公司的旗艦產品。"],["flawed","/flɔːd/","adj.","有瑕疵的、有缺陷的","The survey method was flawed.","這項調查方法有缺陷。"],["fulfill","/fʊlˈfɪl/","v.","履行、滿足；完成（訂單）","We were unable to fulfill the large order on time.","我們無法準時完成這筆大訂單。"],["hype","/haɪp/","n./v.","大肆宣傳；炒作","The product failed to live up to the hype.","這項產品名不副實，辜負了宣傳。"],["infomercial","/ˌɪnfoʊˈmɜːrʃl/","n.","資訊型廣告、購物頻道廣告","The blender was first sold through a late-night infomercial.","這台果汁機最初是透過深夜資訊型廣告販售的。"],["irresistible","/ˌɪrɪˈzɪstəbl/","adj.","難以抗拒的","The discount made the offer irresistible.","這個折扣讓優惠令人難以抗拒。"],["layaway","/ˈleɪəweɪ/","n.","分期預付取貨","You can put the sofa on layaway and pay monthly.","您可以用分期預付方式買沙發，每月付款。"],["lifetime warranty","/ˌlaɪftaɪm ˈwɔːrənti/","phr.","終身保固","The knives come with a lifetime warranty.","這組刀具享終身保固。"],["mail-order","/ˈmeɪl ˌɔːrdər/","adj.","郵購的","The company started as a small mail-order business.","這家公司最初是一家小型郵購公司。"],["medium","/ˈmiːdiəm/","n.","媒介、手段（複數 media）","Radio is still a useful advertising medium.","廣播仍是有用的廣告媒介。"],["no-frills","/ˌnoʊ ˈfrɪlz/","adj.","陽春的、無附加服務的","The no-frills airline keeps its fares low.","這家陽春型航空保持低票價。"],["notable","/ˈnoʊtəbl/","adj.","值得注意的、顯著的","There was a notable increase in online orders.","網路訂單有顯著增加。"],["offering","/ˈɔːfərɪŋ/","n.","（推出的）產品、服務","The new menu offerings are popular with diners.","新推出的菜色很受用餐者歡迎。"],["on hand","/ɑːn ˈhænd/","phr.","現有的、在手邊","We have plenty of stock on hand for the sale.","我們手邊有充足庫存供特賣使用。"],["outsell","/ˌaʊtˈsel/","v.","賣得比…多","Our tablet now outsells all other brands.","我們的平板現在賣得比其他品牌都好。"],["positioning","/pəˈzɪʃənɪŋ/","n.","（品牌、產品）定位","The brand's positioning is clear: quality at a fair price.","這個品牌的定位很清楚：合理價格的高品質。"],["product placement","/ˈprɑːdʌkt ˌpleɪsmənt/","phr.","置入性行銷","The phone appeared in the film through product placement.","這支手機透過置入性行銷出現在電影中。"],["promising","/ˈprɑːmɪsɪŋ/","adj.","有前途的、有希望的","Early sales of the product look promising.","這項產品初期銷售看起來前景不錯。"],["proprietor","/prəˈpraɪətər/","n.","業主、店主","The proprietor personally handles all complaints.","店主親自處理所有客訴。"],["rapport","/ræˈpɔːr/","n.","融洽關係","Good salespeople build rapport with their clients.","優秀的業務員會與客戶建立良好關係。"],["refurbished","/ˌriːˈfɜːrbɪʃt/","adj.","翻新的、整新的","Refurbished laptops are sold at a lower price.","整新筆電以較低價格販售。"],["sample size","/ˈsæmpl saɪz/","phr.","樣本數","The sample size of the survey was too small.","這項調查的樣本數太小。"],["sensational","/senˈseɪʃənl/","adj.","轟動的、聳動的","The ad made sensational claims about the product.","這則廣告對產品做了聳動的宣稱。"],["stand behind","/ˌstænd bɪˈhaɪnd/","phr.","支持、為…擔保","We stand behind every product we sell.","我們為所賣的每件產品擔保。"],["strategic","/strəˈtiːdʒɪk/","adj.","策略性的","The store is in a strategic location near the station.","這家店位於車站附近的戰略位置。"],["tailor","/ˈteɪlər/","v.","使合適、量身打造","We tailor our services to each client's needs.","我們依每位客戶的需求量身打造服務。"],["tailor-made","/ˌteɪlər ˈmeɪd/","adj.","量身訂製的","We offer tailor-made marketing plans.","我們提供量身訂製的行銷方案。"],["tie-in","/ˈtaɪ ɪn/","n.","搭配商品、聯名合作","The cereal is a tie-in with the new movie.","這款穀片是與新電影的聯名商品。"],["amenity","/əˈmenəti/","n.","便利設施","The mall's amenities include free Wi-Fi and lockers.","購物中心的便利設施包括免費無線網路和置物櫃。"],["array","/əˈreɪ/","n.","一系列、大量","The shop offers a wide array of local products.","這家店提供琳瑯滿目的在地產品。"],["assure","/əˈʃʊr/","v.","向…保證、使放心","We assure you that the problem will be fixed.","我們向您保證問題會被解決。"],["attribute","/əˈtrɪbjuːt/","v.","把…歸因於","We attribute the sales increase to our new ad.","我們把銷售成長歸功於新廣告。"],["boycott","/ˈbɔɪkɑːt/","v./n.","抵制","Some consumers boycotted the brand after the scandal.","醜聞後有些消費者抵制該品牌。"],["circulation","/ˌsɜːrkjəˈleɪʃn/","n.","發行量；流通","The magazine has a circulation of 50,000.","這本雜誌發行量為五萬份。"],["consumer confidence","/kənˌsuːmər ˈkɑːnfɪdəns/","phr.","消費者信心","Consumer confidence fell for the third month.","消費者信心連續第三個月下滑。"],["copywriter","/ˈkɑːpiraɪtər/","n.","廣告文案撰寫人","The copywriter came up with a clever slogan.","文案人員想出了一句巧妙的標語。"],["demographics","/ˌdeməˈɡræfɪks/","n.","人口統計資料；客層特徵","We studied the demographics of our online shoppers.","我們研究了網路購物者的人口統計資料。"],["descriptive","/dɪˈskrɪptɪv/","adj.","描述性的","Write descriptive product titles to attract buyers.","撰寫具描述性的商品標題以吸引買家。"],["discreet","/dɪˈskriːt/","adj.","謹慎的、低調的","Staff should be discreet when handling complaints.","處理客訴時員工應謹慎低調。"],["endorser","/ɪnˈdɔːrsər/","n.","代言人","The athlete is a well-known endorser of sports drinks.","這位運動員是知名的運動飲料代言人。"],["entice","/ɪnˈtaɪs/","v.","誘使、吸引","Free gifts are used to entice new customers.","免費禮物被用來吸引新顧客。"],["fine print","/ˈfaɪn prɪnt/","phr.","（合約、廣告的）細則","Read the fine print before accepting the offer.","接受優惠前請先詳閱細則。"],["foot traffic","/ˈfʊt ˌtræfɪk/","phr.","來店人潮、人流","The new subway station increased foot traffic.","新捷運站增加了來店人潮。"],["garment","/ˈɡɑːrmənt/","n.","衣服、服裝（一件）","Each garment is checked for quality before shipping.","每件衣服出貨前都經過品質檢查。"],["haggle","/ˈhæɡl/","v.","討價還價","Customers often haggle over prices at the market.","顧客在市場上常常討價還價。"],["hard sell","/ˌhɑːrd ˈsel/","phr.","強迫推銷","Customers dislike the hard sell.","顧客不喜歡強迫推銷。"],["incompatible","/ˌɪnkəmˈpætəbl/","adj.","不相容的","The charger is incompatible with older models.","這個充電器與舊型號不相容。"],["make up for","/ˌmeɪk ˈʌp fɔːr/","phr.","彌補","We gave her a voucher to make up for the delay.","我們給她一張禮券來彌補延誤。"],["market penetration","/ˌmɑːrkɪt ˌpenəˈtreɪʃn/","phr.","市場滲透（率）","Low prices helped our market penetration in Asia.","低價幫助我們打入亞洲市場。"],["minimize","/ˈmɪnɪmaɪz/","v.","使最小化、降到最低","We aim to minimize customer waiting time.","我們致力於讓顧客等待時間降到最低。"],["misleading","/ˌmɪsˈliːdɪŋ/","adj.","誤導的","The company was fined for misleading advertising.","這家公司因不實廣告被罰款。"],["mock-up","/ˈmɑːk ʌp/","n.","實體模型、樣稿","The designer showed us a mock-up of the new package.","設計師給我們看了新包裝的樣稿。"],["modest","/ˈmɑːdɪst/","adj.","適度的、不大的","Sales showed a modest increase last quarter.","上一季銷售小幅成長。"],["niche market","/ˈniːʃ ˌmɑːrkɪt/","phr.","利基市場","The shop serves a niche market of vintage collectors.","這家店服務復古收藏家的利基市場。"],["on backorder","/ɑːn ˈbækɔːrdər/","phr.","缺貨待補","The item is on backorder for two weeks.","這項商品缺貨，需等兩週。"],["out of print","/ˌaʊt əv ˈprɪnt/","phr.","絕版的","That catalog is now out of print.","那本型錄現已絕版。"],["overwhelming","/ˌoʊvərˈwelmɪŋ/","adj.","壓倒性的、極大的","The response to the sale was overwhelming.","特賣的反應極為熱烈。"],["prime time","/ˈpraɪm taɪm/","phr.","黃金時段","Ads during prime time are very expensive.","黃金時段的廣告非常昂貴。"],["proposition","/ˌprɑːpəˈzɪʃn/","n.","提議、主張；（商業）方案","Our value proposition is fast and free delivery.","我們的價值主張是快速免費送貨。"],["public opinion","/ˌpʌblɪk əˈpɪnjən/","phr.","輿論、民意","Public opinion turned against the company.","輿論轉而對公司不利。"],["radio spot","/ˈreɪdioʊ spɑːt/","phr.","廣播廣告時段","We bought a thirty-second radio spot.","我們買了一則三十秒的廣播廣告。"],["reliability","/rɪˌlaɪəˈbɪləti/","n.","可靠性","The brand is known for its reliability.","這個品牌以可靠著稱。"],["revamp","/ˌriːˈvæmp/","v./n.","改造、翻新","We plan to revamp our website this summer.","我們計畫今年夏天改版網站。"],["sizable","/ˈsaɪzəbl/","adj.","相當大的","The ad campaign required a sizable budget.","這次廣告活動需要相當大的預算。"],["spokesman","/ˈspoʊksmən/","n.","發言人（男）","A company spokesman denied the rumors.","一位公司發言人否認了傳聞。"],["spur","/spɜːr/","v./n.","刺激、激勵","Lower prices spurred demand for the product.","降價刺激了該產品的需求。"],["stall","/stɔːl/","n./v.","攤位；停滯","She runs a fruit stall at the night market.","她在夜市經營一個水果攤。"],["superb","/suːˈpɜːrb/","adj.","極好的","The hotel received superb reviews from guests.","這家飯店獲得房客極高的評價。"],["sweepstakes","/ˈswiːpsteɪks/","n.","抽獎活動","Enter our sweepstakes for a chance to win a car.","參加我們的抽獎就有機會贏得汽車。"],["tasteful","/ˈteɪstfl/","adj.","有品味的、雅致的","The store's decorations are simple and tasteful.","這家店的裝潢簡單又有品味。"],["top-notch","/ˌtɑːp ˈnɑːtʃ/","adj.","一流的","We pride ourselves on top-notch customer service.","我們以一流的客戶服務自豪。"],["trade name","/ˈtreɪd neɪm/","phr.","商品名稱、商號","The drug is sold under a different trade name.","這種藥以不同的商品名稱販售。"],["upsell","/ˌʌpˈsel/","v.","追加銷售、向上銷售","Waiters are encouraged to upsell desserts.","服務生被鼓勵加推甜點。"],["usage","/ˈjuːsɪdʒ/","n.","使用（量）、用法","App usage rose sharply after the update.","更新後應用程式使用量大增。"],["voice a complaint","/ˌvɔɪs ə kəmˈpleɪnt/","phr.","提出抱怨","Several guests voiced complaints about the noise.","幾位客人對噪音提出抱怨。"],["word of mouth","/ˌwɜːrd əv ˈmaʊθ/","phr.","口碑、口耳相傳","Most of our new customers come through word of mouth.","我們的新客戶大多來自口碑。"],["brand ambassador","/ˈbrænd æmˌbæsədər/","phr.","品牌大使","The singer was named the brand ambassador for Asia.","這位歌手被任命為亞洲區品牌大使。"],["brand identity","/ˈbrænd aɪˌdentəti/","phr.","品牌識別","Our logo and colors form a strong brand identity.","我們的標誌與色彩形成鮮明的品牌識別。"],["rebrand","/ˌriːˈbrænd/","v.","重塑品牌","The company decided to rebrand to attract younger buyers.","公司決定重塑品牌以吸引年輕買家。"],["consumer trend","/kənˌsuːmər ˈtrend/","phr.","消費趨勢","Healthy eating is a growing consumer trend.","健康飲食是日漸興起的消費趨勢。"],["market analysis","/ˌmɑːrkɪt əˈnæləsɪs/","phr.","市場分析","The report includes a detailed market analysis.","報告中包含詳細的市場分析。"],["competitive edge","/kəmˌpetətɪv ˈedʒ/","phr.","競爭優勢","Fast delivery gives us a competitive edge.","快速送貨給了我們競爭優勢。"],["unique selling point","/juˌniːk ˈselɪŋ pɔɪnt/","phr.","獨特賣點","Its unique selling point is a ten-year guarantee.","它的獨特賣點是十年保證。"],["buying habits","/ˈbaɪɪŋ ˌhæbɪts/","phr.","購買習慣","The pandemic changed consumers' buying habits.","疫情改變了消費者的購買習慣。"],["bargain hunter","/ˈbɑːrɡən ˌhʌntər/","phr.","愛撿便宜的人","Bargain hunters lined up early for the sale.","愛撿便宜的人一早就來排隊等特賣。"],["affordability","/əˌfɔːrdəˈbɪləti/","n.","可負擔性、價格親民","Affordability is the main reason customers choose us.","價格親民是顧客選擇我們的主因。"],["test market","/ˈtest ˌmɑːrkɪt/","n./v.","試銷市場；試銷","We will test market the drink in two cities.","我們將在兩個城市試銷這款飲料。"],["soft launch","/ˈsɔːft lɔːntʃ/","phr.","試營運、低調試推","The app had a soft launch in Taiwan first.","這款應用程式先在台灣試推。"],["airtime","/ˈertaɪm/","n.","播出時間","The company bought airtime on three TV channels.","公司在三個電視頻道購買了播出時段。"],["mystery shopper","/ˌmɪstəri ˈʃɑːpər/","phr.","神秘客","A mystery shopper checks our service every month.","每個月都有神秘客來檢查我們的服務。"],["patronize","/ˈpeɪtrənaɪz/","v.","光顧、惠顧","Thank you for patronizing our store.","感謝您光顧本店。"],["consign","/kənˈsaɪn/","v.","託運、寄送","The goods were consigned to our Osaka office.","貨物已託運至我們的大阪辦公室。"],["consignee","/ˌkɑːnsaɪˈniː/","n.","收貨人","The consignee must sign the delivery receipt.","收貨人必須在送貨單上簽名。"],["declaration","/ˌdekləˈreɪʃən/","n.","申報（單）；宣告","Fill out the customs declaration form.","填寫海關申報單。"],["quarantine","/ˈkwɔːrəntiːn/","n./v.","檢疫；隔離","The plants were held in quarantine for a week.","這批植物被檢疫扣留了一週。"],["embargo","/ɪmˈbɑːrɡoʊ/","n.","禁運","The embargo stopped all trade with that country.","禁運使與該國的所有貿易停止。"],["certify","/ˈsɜːrtɪfaɪ/","v.","證明、認證","This lab certifies the safety of toys.","這間實驗室負責認證玩具安全。"],["hazardous","/ˈhæzərdəs/","adj.","有危險的、有害的","Hazardous materials need special labels.","危險物品需要特殊標籤。"],["dispose","/dɪˈspoʊz/","v.","處置、丟棄（常接 of）","Dispose of chemical waste properly.","化學廢料要妥善處理。"],["disposal","/dɪˈspoʊzəl/","n.","處理、處置","Waste disposal costs have increased.","廢棄物處理費用增加了。"],["textile","/ˈtekstaɪl/","n.","紡織品","The company exports textiles to Europe.","這家公司出口紡織品到歐洲。"],["semiconductor","/ˌsemikənˈdʌktər/","n.","半導體","Taiwan leads the world in semiconductor production.","台灣在半導體生產上領先全球。"],["modification","/ˌmɑːdɪfɪˈkeɪʃən/","n.","修改、改裝","The design needs a few modifications.","這個設計需要一些修改。"],["calibrate","/ˈkælɪbreɪt/","v.","校準","The scales are calibrated every month.","磅秤每個月都會校準。"],["precision","/prɪˈsɪʒən/","n.","精確、精密","These parts are cut with great precision.","這些零件切割得非常精密。"],["consistency","/kənˈsɪstənsi/","n.","一致性","Consistency is key to quality control.","一致性是品管的關鍵。"],["functional","/ˈfʌŋkʃənəl/","adj.","功能性的；可運作的","The machine is old but still functional.","機器雖舊但仍可運作。"],["mechanism","/ˈmekənɪzəm/","n.","機械裝置；機制","The locking mechanism is broken.","鎖定裝置壞了。"],["conveyor","/kənˈveɪər/","n.","輸送機","Boxes travel by conveyor to the loading area.","箱子由輸送機送到裝貨區。"],["lever","/ˈlevər/","n.","操縱桿、槓桿","Pull the lever to release the brake.","拉下操縱桿以鬆開煞車。"],["inventory control","/ˈɪnvəntɔːri kənˌtroʊl/","n.","庫存管理","Good inventory control reduces waste.","良好的庫存管理可以減少浪費。"],["stocktaking","/ˈstɑːkteɪkɪŋ/","n.","盤點存貨","The store closes early for stocktaking.","店家為了盤點提早打烊。"],["log","/lɔːɡ/","n./v.","紀錄、日誌；記錄","Log every repair in the maintenance book.","每次維修都要記錄在保養簿上。"],["protocol","/ˈproʊtəkɔːl/","n.","規程、協定","Follow the safety protocol at all times.","隨時遵守安全規程。"],["throughput","/ˈθruːpʊt/","n.","產出量、處理量","The new system increased warehouse throughput.","新系統提高了倉庫的處理量。"],["union","/ˈjuːnjən/","n.","工會","The union asked for safer working conditions.","工會要求更安全的工作環境。"],["lay out","/ˌleɪ ˈaʊt/","phr.","安排、布置；陳列","They laid out the factory to save space.","他們規劃工廠配置以節省空間。"],["line up","/ˌlaɪn ˈʌp/","phr.","排列；安排好","We've lined up a new supplier.","我們已經找好新的供應商了。"],["hook up","/ˌhʊk ˈʌp/","phr.","連接（電源、設備）","The technician hooked up the new printer.","技師把新印表機接好了。"],["phase in","/ˌfeɪz ˈɪn/","phr.","逐步導入","The new system will be phased in over a year.","新系統將在一年內逐步導入。"],["en route","/ˌɑːn ˈruːt/","adv.","在途中","The shipment is en route to Singapore.","這批貨正在運往新加坡的途中。"],["freight forwarder","/ˈfreɪt ˌfɔːrwərdər/","n.","貨運承攬業者","Our freight forwarder handles customs for us.","我們的貨運承攬商替我們辦理報關。"],["estimated time of arrival","/ˌestɪmeɪtɪd ˌtaɪm əv əˈraɪvəl/","phr.","預計抵達時間（ETA）","What is the estimated time of arrival?","預計抵達時間是什麼時候？"],["proof of delivery","/ˌpruːf əv dɪˈlɪvəri/","phr.","交貨證明、簽收證明","The driver will send a proof of delivery.","司機會傳送簽收證明。"],["purchase requisition","/ˈpɜːrtʃəs ˌrekwɪˈzɪʃən/","n.","請購單","Submit a purchase requisition for new tools.","購買新工具請提交請購單。"],["stockpile","/ˈstɑːkpaɪl/","n./v.","儲備；囤積","The factory has a stockpile of raw materials.","工廠有一批原料儲備。"],["inventory turnover","/ˈɪnvəntɔːri ˈtɜːrnoʊvər/","n.","存貨週轉率","High inventory turnover means strong sales.","存貨週轉率高代表銷售強勁。"],["logistical","/ləˈdʒɪstɪkəl/","adj.","物流的；後勤的","We faced several logistical problems.","我們遇到了幾個物流上的問題。"],["hauling","/ˈhɔːlɪŋ/","n.","貨運、拖運","The company specializes in long-distance hauling.","這家公司專做長途貨運。"],["freight charge","/ˈfreɪt tʃɑːrdʒ/","n.","運費","The freight charge is paid by the buyer.","運費由買方支付。"],["payload","/ˈpeɪloʊd/","n.","載重量、有效載荷","The truck's payload is ten tons.","這台卡車的載重是十噸。"],["load capacity","/ˈloʊd kəˌpæsəti/","n.","承載量","Do not exceed the shelf's load capacity.","不要超過架子的承載量。"],["transshipment","/trænsˈʃɪpmənt/","n.","轉運","The goods go through transshipment in Hong Kong.","貨物在香港轉運。"],["port of entry","/ˌpɔːrt əv ˈentri/","phr.","入境港口","Keelung is the port of entry for this cargo.","基隆是這批貨的入境港口。"],["country of origin","/ˌkʌntri əv ˈɔːrɪdʒɪn/","phr.","原產國","The label must show the country of origin.","標籤上必須標示原產國。"],["mishandle","/ˌmɪsˈhændl/","v.","處理不當","The parcel was mishandled by the carrier.","包裹被貨運商處理不當。"],["insured","/ɪnˈʃʊrd/","adj.","已投保的","The shipment is fully insured.","這批貨已全額投保。"],["criterion","/kraɪˈtɪriən/","n.","標準、準則（複數 criteria）","Price is not our only criterion for choosing suppliers.","價格不是我們選擇供應商的唯一標準。"],["meet standards","/ˌmiːt ˈstændərdz/","phr.","符合標準","All our products meet international standards.","我們所有產品都符合國際標準。"],["variation","/ˌveriˈeɪʃən/","n.","變化、差異","There is little variation in product size.","產品尺寸的差異很小。"],["deviation","/ˌdiːviˈeɪʃən/","n.","偏差、偏離","Any deviation from the spec must be reported.","任何偏離規格的情況都必須回報。"],["lean","/liːn/","adj.","精實的；精簡的","We adopted lean manufacturing last year.","我們去年導入了精實生產。"],["just-in-time","/ˌdʒʌst ɪn ˈtaɪm/","adj.","及時（生產）的、零庫存的","A just-in-time system keeps inventory low.","及時生產系統能讓庫存維持在低水位。"],["small-scale","/ˌsmɔːl ˈskeɪl/","adj.","小規模的","They began as a small-scale workshop.","他們從一間小規模工作坊起家。"],["made-to-order","/ˌmeɪd tu ˈɔːrdər/","adj.","接單生產的、訂製的","All our furniture is made-to-order.","我們所有家具都是接單訂製的。"],["off-the-shelf","/ˌɔːf ðə ˈʃelf/","adj.","現成的、標準規格的","We use off-the-shelf parts to save money.","我們使用現成零件來省錢。"],["offshore","/ˌɔːfˈʃɔːr/","adv.","在海外","Many firms moved production offshore.","許多公司把生產移到海外。"],["mill","/mɪl/","n.","工廠（紡織、造紙、鋼鐵等）；磨坊","The paper mill employs 300 people.","這間造紙廠雇用三百人。"],["fulfillment center","/fʊlˈfɪlmənt ˌsentər/","n.","訂單履行中心、出貨中心","Orders are packed at our fulfillment center.","訂單在我們的出貨中心包裝。"],["dispatcher","/dɪˈspætʃər/","n.","調度員","The dispatcher assigns routes to the drivers.","調度員分配路線給司機。"],["third-party","/ˌθɜːrd ˈpɑːrti/","adj.","第三方的","We hired a third-party logistics company.","我們聘請了第三方物流公司。"],["logistics provider","/ləˈdʒɪstɪks prəˌvaɪdər/","n.","物流業者","Our logistics provider stores goods in five cities.","我們的物流業者在五個城市存放貨品。"],["supply agreement","/səˈplaɪ əˌɡriːmənt/","n.","供貨協議","We signed a two-year supply agreement.","我們簽了一份兩年的供貨協議。"],["long-term contract","/ˌlɔːŋ tɜːrm ˈkɑːntrækt/","n.","長期合約","A long-term contract secures steady prices.","長期合約可確保價格穩定。"],["interruption","/ˌɪntəˈrʌpʃən/","n.","中斷","There was a brief interruption in supply.","供貨曾短暫中斷。"],["production volume","/prəˈdʌkʃən ˌvɑːljuːm/","n.","生產量","Production volume rose by ten percent.","生產量增加了百分之十。"],["production target","/prəˈdʌkʃən ˌtɑːrɡɪt/","n.","生產目標","We met our production target for the quarter.","我們達成了本季的生產目標。"],["yield rate","/ˈjiːld reɪt/","n.","良率","The new process improved the yield rate.","新製程提升了良率。"],["defective item","/dɪˈfektɪv ˈaɪtəm/","n.","瑕疵品","Defective items will be replaced free of charge.","瑕疵品將免費更換。"],["manufacturing process","/ˌmænjəˈfæktʃərɪŋ ˌprɑːses/","n.","製造流程、製程","We improved the manufacturing process.","我們改善了製造流程。"],["manufacturing facility","/ˌmænjəˈfæktʃərɪŋ fəˌsɪləti/","n.","製造廠、生產設施","The firm opened a manufacturing facility in Thailand.","這家公司在泰國設立了生產設施。"],["mold","/moʊld/","n.","模具；黴菌","A new mold costs about $20,000.","一套新模具大約兩萬美元。"],["casting","/ˈkæstɪŋ/","n.","鑄造；鑄件","The castings are cleaned before machining.","鑄件在加工前會先清理。"],["welding","/ˈweldɪŋ/","n.","焊接","Welding must be done in a safe area.","焊接必須在安全區域進行。"],["weld","/weld/","v.","焊接","The workers welded the frame together.","工人把框架焊接起來。"],["finish","/ˈfɪnɪʃ/","n.","表面處理、塗裝","The table has a smooth finish.","這張桌子表面處理很光滑。"],["fitting","/ˈfɪtɪŋ/","n.","配件、接頭","Replace the leaking pipe fitting.","更換漏水的管接頭。"],["apparatus","/ˌæpəˈrætəs/","n.","儀器、設備","The lab bought new testing apparatus.","實驗室購入了新的測試設備。"],["timber","/ˈtɪmbər/","n.","木材、木料","The timber is imported from Canada.","這些木材是從加拿大進口的。"],["petroleum","/pəˈtroʊliəm/","n.","石油","Plastic is made from petroleum.","塑膠是由石油製成的。"],["refinery","/rɪˈfaɪnəri/","n.","煉油廠；精煉廠","The refinery processes crude oil.","煉油廠處理原油。"],["refine","/rɪˈfaɪn/","v.","精煉；改進","The company refines sugar for export.","這家公司精煉糖供出口。"],["extract","/ɪkˈstrækt/","v.","提取、開採","The firm extracts copper from the mine.","這家公司從礦場開採銅礦。"],["processing plant","/ˈprɑːsesɪŋ plænt/","n.","加工廠","The fish are packed at a processing plant.","魚在加工廠包裝。"],["bottling plant","/ˈbɑːtlɪŋ plænt/","n.","裝瓶廠","The bottling plant fills 5,000 bottles an hour.","裝瓶廠每小時裝填五千瓶。"],["barrel","/ˈbærəl/","n.","桶；一桶（石油計量單位）","Oil prices fell to $70 a barrel.","油價跌到每桶七十美元。"],["drum","/drʌm/","n.","大圓桶","The chemicals are stored in steel drums.","化學品存放在鋼製圓桶中。"],["sack","/sæk/","n.","大袋、麻袋","The rice comes in 50-kilogram sacks.","米以五十公斤裝的大袋供應。"],["cargo hold","/ˈkɑːrɡoʊ hoʊld/","n.","貨艙","The boxes were stored in the cargo hold.","箱子存放在貨艙裡。"],["shipload","/ˈʃɪploʊd/","n.","一船的貨量","A shipload of grain arrived yesterday.","一整船的穀物昨天抵達。"],["picking","/ˈpɪkɪŋ/","n.","揀貨","Picking errors have dropped since we installed scanners.","裝了掃描器後揀貨錯誤減少了。"],["picker","/ˈpɪkər/","n.","揀貨員","Each picker fills about 100 orders a day.","每位揀貨員一天處理約一百筆訂單。"],["labeling","/ˈleɪbəlɪŋ/","n.","貼標；標示","Proper labeling is required by law.","法律規定必須正確標示。"],["cubic","/ˈkjuːbɪk/","adj.","立方的","The container holds 33 cubic meters.","這個貨櫃容量為三十三立方公尺。"],["square meter","/ˌskwer ˈmiːtər/","n.","平方公尺","The warehouse covers 5,000 square meters.","倉庫占地五千平方公尺。"],["best before","/ˌbest bɪˈfɔːr/","phr.","最佳賞味期限","Check the best before date on the package.","查看包裝上的最佳賞味日期。"],["temperature-controlled","/ˈtemprətʃər kənˌtroʊld/","adj.","溫控的","Vaccines are shipped in temperature-controlled containers.","疫苗以溫控貨櫃運送。"],["cold storage","/ˌkoʊld ˈstɔːrɪdʒ/","n.","冷藏庫、冷藏","The seafood is kept in cold storage.","海鮮存放在冷藏庫。"],["spoilage","/ˈspɔɪlɪdʒ/","n.","腐壞、損耗","Better packaging reduced spoilage.","更好的包裝減少了腐壞損耗。"],["contamination","/kənˌtæmɪˈneɪʃən/","n.","污染","The batch was destroyed due to contamination.","這一批因遭受污染而被銷毀。"],["sanitary","/ˈsænɪteri/","adj.","衛生的","The kitchen must meet sanitary standards.","廚房必須符合衛生標準。"],["sterile","/ˈsterəl/","adj.","無菌的","The tools are kept in a sterile room.","工具存放在無菌室。"],["clean room","/ˈkliːn ruːm/","n.","無塵室","Workers wear special suits in the clean room.","工人在無塵室裡穿著特殊服裝。"],["occupational safety","/ˌɑːkjəˌpeɪʃənəl ˈseɪfti/","n.","職業安全","The course covers occupational safety rules.","課程涵蓋職業安全規定。"],["work-related","/ˈwɜːrk rɪˌleɪtɪd/","adj.","與工作相關的","Work-related injuries have decreased.","職業傷害已經減少。"],["hazardous materials","/ˌhæzərdəs məˈtɪriəlz/","n.","危險物品","Hazardous materials need special handling.","危險物品需要特殊處理。"],["fume","/fjuːm/","n.","（有害）氣體、煙霧","Avoid breathing in the fumes.","避免吸入這些氣體。"],["exhaust","/ɪɡˈzɔːst/","n.","廢氣、排氣","Truck exhaust is a source of pollution.","卡車廢氣是污染源之一。"],["noise level","/ˈnɔɪz ˌlevəl/","n.","噪音值","Noise levels in the plant are monitored.","廠內的噪音值受到監測。"],["voltage","/ˈvoʊltɪdʒ/","n.","電壓","Check the voltage before plugging it in.","插電前先確認電壓。"],["circuit","/ˈsɜːrkɪt/","n.","電路","A short circuit caused the fire.","短路引起了火災。"],["reboot","/ˌriːˈbuːt/","v.","重新開機","Reboot the system after installing the update.","安裝更新後重新開機。"],["operating manual","/ˈɑːpəreɪtɪŋ ˌmænjuəl/","n.","操作手冊","Keep the operating manual near the machine.","操作手冊請放在機器旁。"],["troubleshooting","/ˈtrʌbəlʃuːtɪŋ/","n.","故障排除","The manual has a troubleshooting section.","手冊裡有故障排除的章節。"],["diagnose","/ˌdaɪəɡˈnoʊs/","v.","診斷（問題）","The technician diagnosed the problem quickly.","技師很快就找出了問題。"],["diagnostic","/ˌdaɪəɡˈnɑːstɪk/","adj.","診斷的","Run a diagnostic test on the system.","對系統執行診斷測試。"],["preventive maintenance","/prɪˌventɪv ˈmeɪntənəns/","n.","預防性保養","Preventive maintenance reduces breakdowns.","預防性保養能減少故障。"],["scheduled maintenance","/ˌskedʒuːld ˈmeɪntənəns/","n.","定期維護","The line will stop for scheduled maintenance.","生產線將因定期維護而停機。"],["maintenance crew","/ˈmeɪntənəns kruː/","n.","維修人員","The maintenance crew works on weekends.","維修人員週末上班。"],["service contract","/ˈsɜːrvɪs ˌkɑːntrækt/","n.","維修服務合約","Our service contract covers all repairs.","我們的維修合約涵蓋所有修理。"],["equipment failure","/ɪˈkwɪpmənt ˌfeɪljər/","n.","設備故障","Equipment failure cost us a day of production.","設備故障讓我們損失一天的產量。"],["heavy equipment","/ˌhevi ɪˈkwɪpmənt/","n.","重型設備","Heavy equipment was brought in to clear the site.","重型設備被運來清理工地。"],["industrialize","/ɪnˈdʌstriəlaɪz/","v.","工業化","The region industrialized quickly in the 1980s.","該地區在一九八○年代迅速工業化。"],["consistent quality","/kənˌsɪstənt ˈkwɑːləti/","n.","穩定的品質","Buyers expect consistent quality.","買方期望品質穩定。"],["quality assurance","/ˈkwɑːləti əˌʃʊrəns/","n.","品質保證（QA）","She manages the quality assurance team.","她負責管理品保團隊。"],["reliable supplier","/rɪˌlaɪəbəl səˈplaɪər/","n.","可靠的供應商","Finding a reliable supplier took months.","找到一家可靠的供應商花了好幾個月。"],["sourcing","/ˈsɔːrsɪŋ/","n.","採購、尋找貨源","He is in charge of sourcing raw materials.","他負責原料採購。"],["subcontractor","/ˈsʌbkɑːntræktər/","n.","轉包商、下包商","A subcontractor makes the plastic parts.","塑膠零件由下包商製造。"],["standing order","/ˌstændɪŋ ˈɔːrdər/","n.","長期訂單、定期訂購","We have a standing order for ink every month.","我們每月都有一筆固定的墨水訂單。"],["outstanding order","/aʊtˌstændɪŋ ˈɔːrdər/","n.","未完成訂單","There are still five outstanding orders.","還有五筆未完成的訂單。"],["restocking fee","/riːˈstɑːkɪŋ fiː/","n.","重新上架費、退貨手續費","A 15% restocking fee applies to returns.","退貨需收取百分之十五的手續費。"],["physical inventory","/ˌfɪzɪkəl ˈɪnvəntɔːri/","n.","實地盤點","We do a physical inventory twice a year.","我們一年做兩次實地盤點。"],["inventory management","/ˈɪnvəntɔːri ˌmænɪdʒmənt/","n.","庫存管理","The software helps with inventory management.","這套軟體有助於庫存管理。"],["stock shortage","/ˈstɑːk ˌʃɔːrtɪdʒ/","n.","缺貨、庫存短缺","A stock shortage delayed several orders.","庫存短缺延誤了幾筆訂單。"],["pilot program","/ˈpaɪlət ˌproʊɡræm/","n.","試辦計畫","The pilot program will run for three months.","試辦計畫將進行三個月。"],["dry run","/ˌdraɪ ˈrʌn/","n.","預演、試跑","Let's do a dry run of the new procedure.","我們來預演一下新流程。"],["leakage","/ˈliːkɪdʒ/","n.","滲漏、漏出","Check the tank for leakage.","檢查油槽是否有滲漏。"],["replace parts","/rɪˌpleɪs ˈpɑːrts/","phr.","更換零件","We replace parts only when necessary.","我們只在必要時更換零件。"],["repairperson","/rɪˈperpɜːrsən/","n.","修理工","A repairperson will come by this afternoon.","今天下午會有修理工來。"],["embark","/ɪmˈbɑːrk/","v.","登（機、船）；著手","Passengers may embark once the ship is cleaned.","船清潔完畢後乘客即可登船。"],["disembark","/ˌdɪsɪmˈbɑːrk/","v.","下（機、船）","Please remain seated until it is time to disembark.","在下機之前請留在座位上。"],["deplane","/diːˈpleɪn/","v.","下飛機","Passengers will deplane through the front door.","乘客將從前門下機。"],["inbound","/ˈɪnbaʊnd/","adj.","入境的、進站的","Inbound flights are delayed because of fog.","入境班機因大霧而延誤。"],["outbound","/ˈaʊtbaʊnd/","adj.","出境的、離站的","The outbound flight leaves at 7:40 a.m.","去程班機早上七點四十分起飛。"],["domestic flight","/dəˌmɛstɪk ˈflaɪt/","n.","國內線班機","Domestic flights depart from Terminal 1.","國內線班機從第一航廈出發。"],["international flight","/ˌɪntɚˌnæʃənəl ˈflaɪt/","n.","國際線班機","Check in three hours early for international flights.","搭國際線請提早三小時報到。"],["red-eye flight","/ˈrɛd aɪ ˌflaɪt/","n.","夜班飛機、紅眼班機","I took a red-eye flight to make the morning meeting.","為了趕上早上的會議，我搭了紅眼班機。"],["frequent flyer","/ˌfriːkwənt ˈflaɪɚ/","n.","飛行常客","Frequent flyers can use the priority check-in lane.","飛行常客可以使用優先報到通道。"],["mileage program","/ˈmaɪlɪdʒ ˌproʊɡræm/","n.","里程計畫","Join our mileage program to earn free flights.","加入我們的里程計畫賺取免費機票。"],["priority boarding","/praɪˌɔːrəti ˈbɔːrdɪŋ/","n.","優先登機","Business class passengers receive priority boarding.","商務艙旅客可優先登機。"],["legroom","/ˈlɛɡruːm/","n.","腿部空間","I paid extra for a seat with more legroom.","我加價買了一個腿部空間較大的座位。"],["recline","/rɪˈklaɪn/","v.","（椅背）向後傾斜","Please do not recline your seat during meal service.","供餐時請勿將椅背後傾。"],["upright position","/ˌʌpraɪt pəˈzɪʃən/","n.","豎直位置","Return your seat to the upright position for landing.","降落時請將椅背豎直。"],["stow","/stoʊ/","v.","收好、存放","Please stow your laptop before takeoff.","起飛前請收好您的筆電。"],["cabin crew","/ˈkæbɪn ˌkruː/","n.","客艙組員","The cabin crew will now demonstrate safety procedures.","客艙組員現在將示範安全程序。"],["air traffic control","/ˌɛr ˈtræfɪk kənˌtroʊl/","n.","航管","The delay was caused by air traffic control.","延誤是航管造成的。"],["grounded","/ˈɡraʊndɪd/","adj.","停飛的","All planes were grounded during the typhoon.","颱風期間所有飛機都停飛了。"],["touch down","/ˌtʌtʃ ˈdaʊn/","phr.","著陸","We touched down in Frankfurt just after midnight.","我們剛過午夜就在法蘭克福降落。"],["transit passenger","/ˈtrænzɪt ˌpæsɪndʒɚ/","n.","過境旅客","Transit passengers should follow the green signs.","過境旅客請依綠色標示前進。"],["immigration form","/ˌɪmɪˈɡreɪʃən ˌfɔːrm/","n.","入境卡","Fill in the immigration form before you land.","降落前請填寫入境卡。"],["entry visa","/ˈɛntri ˌviːzə/","n.","入境簽證","Some countries issue an entry visa on arrival.","有些國家提供落地簽證。"],["visa on arrival","/ˌviːzə ɑːn əˈraɪvəl/","phr.","落地簽證","Visitors can get a visa on arrival at the airport.","旅客可在機場辦理落地簽證。"],["prohibited items","/proʊˌhɪbɪtɪd ˈaɪtəmz/","n.","違禁物品","Prohibited items will be removed at security.","違禁物品會在安檢時被沒收。"],["customs officer","/ˈkʌstəmz ˌɔːfɪsɚ/","n.","海關人員","The customs officer asked to see my receipts.","海關人員要求看我的收據。"],["oversized","/ˌoʊvɚˈsaɪzd/","adj.","超大的","Oversized baggage must be checked at Counter 10.","超大行李須在十號櫃台託運。"],["mishandled baggage","/mɪsˌhændəld ˈbæɡɪdʒ/","n.","遺失或延誤的行李","Report mishandled baggage at the airline's service desk.","行李遺失或延誤請到航空公司服務台申報。"],["travel voucher","/ˈtrævəl ˌvaʊtʃɚ/","n.","旅遊抵用券","The airline gave us a travel voucher for the delay.","航空公司因延誤給了我們旅遊抵用券。"],["lodging allowance","/ˈlɑːdʒɪŋ əˌlaʊəns/","n.","住宿津貼","The daily lodging allowance is 4,000 dollars.","每日住宿津貼為四千元。"],["travel allowance","/ˈtrævəl əˌlaʊəns/","n.","差旅津貼","Employees receive a travel allowance for each trip.","員工每次出差可領取差旅津貼。"],["travel policy","/ˈtrævəl ˌpɑːləsi/","n.","差旅規定","Our travel policy requires economy class for short flights.","我們的差旅規定短程航班須搭經濟艙。"],["preapproval","/ˌpriːəˈpruːvəl/","n.","事先核准","All overseas trips require preapproval from a manager.","所有海外出差都需主管事先核准。"],["in-room","/ˈɪn ruːm/","adj.","房內的","In-room dining is available 24 hours a day.","房內用餐全天候提供。"],["turndown service","/ˈtɝːndaʊn ˌsɝːvɪs/","n.","開夜床服務","Turndown service is offered every evening.","每晚提供開夜床服務。"],["hospitality","/ˌhɑːspɪˈtæləti/","n.","款待；餐旅業","Thank you for your warm hospitality during our visit.","感謝您在我們拜訪期間的熱情款待。"],["hospitality industry","/ˌhɑːspɪˈtæləti ˌɪndəstri/","n.","餐旅業","She has ten years of experience in the hospitality industry.","她在餐旅業有十年經驗。"],["hotelier","/ˌoʊtəlˈjeɪ/","n.","飯店經營者","The hotelier plans to open three new properties.","那位飯店經營者計畫開設三家新飯店。"],["guesthouse","/ˈɡɛsthaʊs/","n.","民宿、賓館","We stayed in a quiet guesthouse near the river.","我們住在河邊一間安靜的民宿。"],["bed and breakfast","/ˌbɛd ən ˈbrɛkfəst/","n.","民宿（附早餐）","The town has several charming bed and breakfasts.","這個小鎮有好幾間迷人的民宿。"],["penthouse","/ˈpɛnthaʊs/","n.","頂樓套房","The penthouse suite has a private terrace.","頂樓套房附有私人露台。"],["adjoining rooms","/əˌdʒɔɪnɪŋ ˈruːmz/","n.","相連房","We requested adjoining rooms for the project team.","我們為專案團隊申請了相連房。"],["non-smoking room","/ˌnɑːn ˈsmoʊkɪŋ ˌruːm/","n.","禁菸房","All our rooms are non-smoking rooms.","我們所有房間都是禁菸房。"],["all-inclusive","/ˌɔːl ɪnˈkluːsɪv/","adj.","全包式的","The resort offers all-inclusive packages.","度假村提供全包式套裝方案。"],["incidentals","/ˌɪnsɪˈdɛntəlz/","n.","雜費","A deposit is required for incidentals at check-in.","入住時需支付雜費押金。"],["cancellation policy","/ˌkænsəˈleɪʃən ˌpɑːləsi/","n.","取消政策","Please read our cancellation policy carefully.","請仔細閱讀我們的取消政策。"],["culinary","/ˈkʌlɪnɛri/","adj.","烹飪的","The chef studied at a famous culinary school.","那位主廚在知名的烹飪學校進修過。"],["gourmet","/ɡʊrˈmeɪ/","adj./n.","美食的；美食家","The hotel restaurant serves gourmet French food.","飯店餐廳供應精緻法式料理。"],["delicacy","/ˈdɛlɪkəsi/","n.","佳餚、珍饈","Stinky tofu is a local delicacy.","臭豆腐是當地特色美食。"],["savory","/ˈseɪvəri/","adj.","鹹香可口的","We offer both sweet and savory pastries.","我們提供甜的和鹹的糕點。"],["palatable","/ˈpælətəbəl/","adj.","可口的；可接受的","The new menu is more palatable to foreign visitors.","新菜單更合外國遊客的口味。"],["appetite","/ˈæpɪtaɪt/","n.","食慾","The long meeting gave everyone a big appetite.","冗長的會議讓大家胃口大開。"],["hors d'oeuvres","/ɔːr ˈdɝːvz/","n.","開胃小點","Hors d'oeuvres will be served during the cocktail hour.","雞尾酒時段將供應開胃小點。"],["cocktail party","/ˈkɑːkteɪl ˌpɑːrti/","n.","雞尾酒會","A cocktail party will follow the awards dinner.","頒獎晚宴後接著舉辦雞尾酒會。"],["banquet facilities","/ˈbæŋkwɪt fəˌsɪlətiz/","n.","宴會設施","The hotel's banquet facilities can serve 500 guests.","飯店的宴會設施可服務五百位賓客。"],["sit-down dinner","/ˌsɪt daʊn ˈdɪnɚ/","n.","正式坐席晚宴","We chose a sit-down dinner instead of a buffet.","我們選了正式坐席晚宴而不是自助餐。"],["seating chart","/ˈsiːtɪŋ ˌtʃɑːrt/","n.","座位表","Please check the seating chart at the entrance.","請查看入口處的座位表。"],["seating arrangement","/ˈsiːtɪŋ əˌreɪndʒmənt/","n.","座位安排","The seating arrangement was changed at the last minute.","座位安排在最後一刻變更了。"],["head table","/ˈhɛd ˌteɪbəl/","n.","主桌","The guest of honor will sit at the head table.","貴賓將坐在主桌。"],["guest of honor","/ˌɡɛst əv ˈɑːnɚ/","n.","貴賓、主賓","The retiring director was the guest of honor.","即將退休的董事是當晚的主賓。"],["toast","/toʊst/","n./v.","敬酒、乾杯","Let's propose a toast to our new partners.","讓我們向新夥伴敬酒。"],["RSVP","/ˌɑːr ɛs viː ˈpiː/","v./n.","回覆是否出席","Please RSVP by Friday so we can plan the meals.","請在週五前回覆是否出席，以便安排餐點。"],["cater an event","/ˌkeɪtɚ ən ɪˈvɛnt/","phr.","為活動供餐","They have catered events for up to 1,000 people.","他們曾為多達千人的活動供餐。"],["food vendor","/ˈfuːd ˌvɛndɚ/","n.","餐飲攤商","Several food vendors will be at the festival.","節慶會場將有數家餐飲攤商。"],["food court","/ˈfuːd ˌkɔːrt/","n.","美食街","The food court is on the basement level.","美食街位於地下樓層。"],["eatery","/ˈiːtəri/","n.","小餐館","There are many small eateries near the office.","辦公室附近有許多小餐館。"],["bistro","/ˈbiːstroʊ/","n.","小酒館、小餐館","We had lunch at a French bistro.","我們在一家法式小餐館吃了午餐。"],["fine dining","/ˌfaɪn ˈdaɪnɪŋ/","n.","高級餐飲","The hotel's fine dining restaurant requires reservations.","飯店的高級餐廳需要訂位。"],["maître d'","/ˌmeɪtrə ˈdiː/","n.","餐廳領班","The maître d' showed us to a table by the window.","領班帶我們到靠窗的桌位。"],["sommelier","/ˌsʌməlˈjeɪ/","n.","侍酒師","The sommelier recommended a wine to go with the fish.","侍酒師推薦了一款適合配魚的酒。"],["symposium","/sɪmˈpoʊziəm/","n.","研討會、座談會","The symposium brought together experts from ten countries.","這場研討會匯集了來自十國的專家。"],["summit","/ˈsʌmɪt/","n.","高峰會","Leaders from the industry met at the annual summit.","業界領袖在年度高峰會上會面。"],["forum","/ˈfɔːrəm/","n.","論壇","The forum focused on green manufacturing.","這場論壇聚焦於綠色製造。"],["plenary session","/ˈpliːnəri ˌsɛʃən/","n.","全體會議","All attendees should join the plenary session at 9 a.m.","所有與會者應參加上午九點的全體會議。"],["moderator","/ˈmɑːdəreɪtɚ/","n.","主持人","The moderator kept the panel discussion on time.","主持人讓座談會準時進行。"],["presenter","/prɪˈzɛntɚ/","n.","報告人、發表者","Each presenter has twenty minutes to speak.","每位報告人有二十分鐘發言。"],["proceedings","/proʊˈsiːdɪŋz/","n.","會議記錄、論文集","The conference proceedings will be published online.","會議論文集將在網路上公布。"],["on-site registration","/ˌɑːn saɪt ˌrɛdʒɪˈstreɪʃən/","n.","現場報名","On-site registration opens at 8 a.m.","現場報名早上八點開始。"],["preregister","/ˌpriːˈrɛdʒɪstɚ/","v.","預先登記","Preregister online to avoid long lines.","事先上網登記以避免大排長龍。"],["lanyard","/ˈlænjɚd/","n.","掛繩","Please wear your badge on the lanyard provided.","請將識別證掛在提供的掛繩上。"],["audiovisual equipment","/ˌɔːdioʊˈvɪʒuəl ɪˌkwɪpmənt/","n.","視聽設備","The venue provides all audiovisual equipment.","場地提供所有視聽設備。"],["lectern","/ˈlɛktɚn/","n.","講台、講桌","The speaker placed his notes on the lectern.","講者把筆記放在講台上。"],["auditorium","/ˌɔːdɪˈtɔːriəm/","n.","禮堂","The keynote speech will take place in the main auditorium.","主題演講將在主禮堂舉行。"],["seating capacity","/ˈsiːtɪŋ kəˌpæsəti/","n.","座位容量","The hall has a seating capacity of 800.","這個廳可容納八百個座位。"],["exhibit space","/ɪɡˈzɪbɪt ˌspeɪs/","n.","展覽空間","Exhibit space is sold by the square meter.","展覽空間以平方公尺計價出售。"],["booth rental","/ˈbuːθ ˌrɛntəl/","n.","攤位租金","Booth rental includes electricity and two chairs.","攤位租金包含電力與兩張椅子。"],["promotional materials","/prəˌmoʊʃənəl məˈtɪriəlz/","n.","宣傳資料","Bring enough promotional materials for three days.","帶足三天份的宣傳資料。"],["lead generation","/ˈliːd dʒɛnəˌreɪʃən/","n.","潛在客戶開發","Trade shows are great for lead generation.","商展很適合開發潛在客戶。"],["networking event","/ˈnɛtwɝːkɪŋ ɪˌvɛnt/","n.","交流活動","I met two potential buyers at a networking event.","我在一場交流活動中認識了兩位潛在買家。"],["mingle","/ˈmɪŋɡəl/","v.","交際、交流","Guests mingled over drinks before dinner.","晚餐前賓客們邊喝飲料邊交流。"],["corporate retreat","/ˌkɔːrpərət rɪˈtriːt/","n.","企業員工旅遊、靜修營","The corporate retreat will take place at a lakeside resort.","企業員工旅遊將在湖畔度假村舉行。"],["incentive trip","/ɪnˈsɛntɪv ˌtrɪp/","n.","獎勵旅遊","Top salespeople earned an incentive trip to Bali.","頂尖業務員贏得了峇里島獎勵旅遊。"],["gala dinner","/ˈɡeɪlə ˌdɪnɚ/","n.","盛大晚宴","The gala dinner will be held on the final night.","盛大晚宴將於最後一晚舉行。"],["fundraiser","/ˈfʌndreɪzɚ/","n.","募款活動","The fundraiser raised two million dollars for the hospital.","那場募款活動為醫院募得兩百萬元。"],["black-tie","/ˌblæk ˈtaɪ/","adj.","須穿正式禮服的","The awards dinner is a black-tie event.","頒獎晚宴是須穿正式禮服的活動。"],["commemorative","/kəˈmɛmərətɪv/","adj.","紀念的","Each guest received a commemorative gift.","每位賓客都收到一份紀念品。"],["festivity","/fɛˈstɪvəti/","n.","慶祝活動","The festivities will continue until midnight.","慶祝活動將持續到午夜。"],["extravaganza","/ɪkˌstrævəˈɡænzə/","n.","盛大表演、盛會","The opening night was a musical extravaganza.","開幕夜是一場盛大的音樂表演。"],["ensemble","/ɑːnˈsɑːmbəl/","n.","合奏團、合唱團","A jazz ensemble played during the reception.","酒會期間有一支爵士樂團演奏。"],["playwright","/ˈpleɪraɪt/","n.","劇作家","The playwright attended the opening performance.","劇作家出席了首演。"],["rehearsal","/rɪˈhɝːsəl/","n.","排練、彩排","There will be a rehearsal the day before the ceremony.","典禮前一天會有彩排。"],["rehearse","/rɪˈhɝːs/","v.","排練","The speakers rehearsed their presentations on stage.","講者們在台上排練簡報。"],["acclaimed","/əˈkleɪmd/","adj.","廣受讚譽的","The dinner features an acclaimed local chef.","晚宴由一位備受讚譽的在地主廚掌廚。"],["captivating","/ˈkæptɪveɪtɪŋ/","adj.","迷人的、引人入勝的","The guest speaker gave a captivating talk.","特邀講者發表了一場引人入勝的演講。"],["curator","/kjʊˈreɪtɚ/","n.","策展人","The curator led a private tour of the gallery.","策展人帶領了一場私人藝廊導覽。"],["heritage site","/ˈhɛrɪtɪdʒ ˌsaɪt/","n.","文化遺產地","The castle is a protected heritage site.","這座城堡是受保護的文化遺產。"],["picturesque","/ˌpɪktʃəˈrɛsk/","adj.","如畫的、風景優美的","The hotel is located in a picturesque village.","飯店位於一個風景如畫的村莊。"],["breathtaking","/ˈbrɛθteɪkɪŋ/","adj.","令人驚嘆的","The view from the top floor is breathtaking.","從頂樓看出去的景色令人驚嘆。"],["secluded","/sɪˈkluːdɪd/","adj.","僻靜的","The resort sits on a secluded beach.","度假村坐落於一處僻靜的海灘。"],["panoramic","/ˌpænəˈræmɪk/","adj.","全景的","The restaurant offers a panoramic view of the city.","餐廳可以眺望城市全景。"],["ecotourism","/ˌiːkoʊˈtʊrɪzəm/","n.","生態旅遊","Ecotourism is growing in rural Taiwan.","生態旅遊在台灣鄉間日漸興盛。"],["backpacker","/ˈbækpækɚ/","n.","背包客","The hostel is popular with young backpackers.","那間青年旅館很受年輕背包客歡迎。"],["sightseer","/ˈsaɪtsiːɚ/","n.","觀光客","The square was crowded with sightseers.","廣場擠滿了觀光客。"],["vacationer","/veɪˈkeɪʃənɚ/","n.","度假者","The island attracts thousands of vacationers each summer.","這座島每年夏天吸引數千名度假者。"],["tourism board","/ˈtʊrɪzəm ˌbɔːrd/","n.","觀光局","The tourism board launched a new ad campaign.","觀光局推出了新的廣告活動。"],["travel advisory","/ˈtrævəl ədˌvaɪzəri/","n.","旅遊警示","Check the travel advisory before visiting the region.","前往該地區前請查看旅遊警示。"],["inclement weather","/ɪnˌklɛmənt ˈwɛðɚ/","n.","惡劣天候","The outdoor event was canceled due to inclement weather.","戶外活動因天候不佳而取消。"],["commuter rail","/kəˈmjuːtɚ ˌreɪl/","n.","通勤鐵路","The commuter rail connects the suburbs to downtown.","通勤鐵路連接郊區與市中心。"],["light rail","/ˌlaɪt ˈreɪl/","n.","輕軌","A new light rail line opens next year.","一條新的輕軌路線將於明年通車。"],["shuttle service","/ˈʃʌtəl ˌsɝːvɪs/","n.","接駁服務","A free shuttle service runs between the hotel and the venue.","飯店與會場之間有免費接駁服務。"],["fare increase","/ˈfɛr ˌɪnkriːs/","n.","票價調漲","The bus company announced a fare increase.","公車公司宣布票價調漲。"],["service disruption","/ˈsɝːvɪs dɪsˌrʌpʃən/","n.","服務中斷","Expect service disruptions on Line 2 this weekend.","本週末二號線預計會有服務中斷。"],["reroute","/ˌriːˈruːt/","v.","改變路線","Buses will be rerouted during the marathon.","馬拉松期間公車將改道行駛。"],["fare evasion","/ˈfɛr ɪˌveɪʒən/","n.","逃票","Fare evasion can result in a heavy fine.","逃票可能被處以高額罰款。"],["pass holder","/ˈpæs ˌhoʊldɚ/","n.","持票人；通行證持有人","Monthly pass holders ride for free on weekends.","月票持有人週末可免費搭乘。"],["vicinity","/vəˈsɪnəti/","n.","附近","There are several hotels in the vicinity of the airport.","機場附近有好幾家飯店。"],["within walking distance","/wɪˌðɪn ˈwɔːkɪŋ ˌdɪstəns/","phr.","走路可到的距離內","The hotel is within walking distance of the venue.","飯店離會場走路就能到。"],["accessible by","/əkˈsɛsəbəl baɪ/","phr.","可經由……抵達","The resort is accessible by ferry only.","那間度假村只能搭渡輪抵達。"],["en suite","/ˌɑːn ˈswiːt/","adj.","（房間）附衛浴的","All bedrooms have en suite bathrooms.","所有臥室都附有衛浴。"],["budget hotel","/ˈbʌdʒɪt hoʊˌtɛl/","n.","平價旅館","Interns usually stay at a budget hotel.","實習生通常住平價旅館。"],["boutique hotel","/buːˈtiːk hoʊˌtɛl/","n.","精品旅館","The team booked a small boutique hotel in Kyoto.","團隊在京都訂了一間小型精品旅館。"],["loyalty member","/ˈlɔɪəlti ˌmɛmbɚ/","n.","會員","Loyalty members get free late check-out.","會員可享免費延遲退房。"],["book in advance","/ˌbʊk ɪn ədˈvæns/","phr.","事先預訂","It's best to book in advance during the trade fair.","商展期間最好提前預訂。"],["check into","/ˌtʃɛk ˈɪntuː/","phr.","入住（飯店）","We checked into the hotel around 9 p.m.","我們大約晚上九點入住飯店。"],["check out of","/ˌtʃɛk ˈaʊt əv/","phr.","退房離開","I need to check out of the hotel by noon.","我必須在中午前退房。"],["see off","/ˌsiː ˈɔːf/","phr.","送行","We went to the airport to see off our visitors.","我們去機場送訪客離開。"],["pick someone up","/ˌpɪk ˌsʌmwʌn ˈʌp/","phr.","接某人","I'll pick you up at the hotel at eight.","我八點去飯店接你。"],["stop over","/ˌstɑːp ˈoʊvɚ/","phr.","中途停留","We'll stop over in Dubai on the way to London.","我們去倫敦途中會在杜拜停留。"],["set off","/ˌsɛt ˈɔːf/","phr.","出發","We set off for the trade show at dawn.","我們天一亮就出發前往商展。"],["get around","/ˌɡɛt əˈraʊnd/","phr.","四處走動、到處去","The easiest way to get around Taipei is by MRT.","在台北最方便的移動方式是搭捷運。"],["tide over","/ˌtaɪd ˈoʊvɚ/","phr.","（食物）讓人撐過一段時間","This snack should tide you over until dinner.","這份點心應該能讓你撐到晚餐。"],["wine and dine","/ˌwaɪn ən ˈdaɪn/","phr.","設宴款待","The supplier wined and dined us during the visit.","拜訪期間供應商設宴款待我們。"],["reconfirm","/ˌriːkənˈfɝːm/","v.","再次確認","Please reconfirm your flight 72 hours before departure.","請在出發前七十二小時再次確認班機。"],["accommodating","/əˈkɑːmədeɪtɪŋ/","adj.","樂於助人的、通融的","The hotel staff were very accommodating.","飯店員工非常樂於協助。"],["hospitable","/hɑːˈspɪtəbəl/","adj.","好客的","Our hosts in Vietnam were extremely hospitable.","我們在越南的東道主非常好客。"],["leasehold","/ˈliːshoʊld/","n./adj.","租賃權；租賃的","The company owns the leasehold on the retail space.","公司擁有該店面的租賃權。"],["sublease","/ˈsʌbliːs/","n./v.","轉租（契約）","We signed a sublease for part of the floor.","我們簽了該樓層部分空間的轉租合約。"],["tenancy","/ˈtenənsi/","n.","租用期間；租賃","Her tenancy ends at the end of the year.","她的租期在年底結束。"],["month-to-month","/ˌmʌnθ tə ˈmʌnθ/","adj.","按月計的","After the first year, the lease becomes month-to-month.","第一年過後，租約改為按月續租。"],["eviction","/ɪˈvɪkʃn/","n.","驅逐、勒令遷出","The tenant received an eviction notice for unpaid rent.","房客因欠租收到驅逐通知。"],["evict","/ɪˈvɪkt/","v.","驅逐（房客）","The landlord cannot evict tenants without notice.","房東不能未經通知就趕走房客。"],["asking price","/ˈæskɪŋ praɪs/","phr.","開價、要價","The asking price for the building is $3 million.","這棟大樓開價三百萬美元。"],["appraiser","/əˈpreɪzər/","n.","估價師","The appraiser valued the house at $450,000.","估價師將房子估價為四十五萬美元。"],["maintenance fee","/ˈmeɪntənəns fiː/","phr.","管理費、維護費","The monthly maintenance fee covers cleaning and security.","每月管理費包含清潔與保全。"],["vacancy rate","/ˈveɪkənsi reɪt/","phr.","空置率","The vacancy rate downtown has dropped sharply.","市中心的空置率大幅下降。"],["fixer-upper","/ˈfɪksər ʌpər/","n.","待整修的房子","They bought a fixer-upper and renovated it.","他們買了一間需整修的房子再加以翻新。"],["curb appeal","/ˈkɜːrb əˌpiːl/","phr.","外觀吸引力","New landscaping improved the building's curb appeal.","新的景觀造景提升了大樓的外觀吸引力。"],["landscaping","/ˈlændskeɪpɪŋ/","n.","景觀美化","The landscaping around the entrance is being redone.","入口周邊的景觀正在重新整理。"],["industrial park","/ɪnˈdʌstriəl pɑːrk/","phr.","工業區","The factory is located in an industrial park.","工廠位於工業區內。"],["retail space","/ˈriːteɪl speɪs/","phr.","零售店面空間","Retail space on the ground floor is available.","一樓有零售店面可出租。"],["high-rise","/ˈhaɪ raɪz/","n./adj.","高樓；高層的","A new high-rise is being built downtown.","市中心正在興建一棟新高樓。"],["atrium","/ˈeɪtriəm/","n.","中庭","The atrium is used for company receptions.","中庭用來舉辦公司酒會。"],["courtyard","/ˈkɔːrtjɑːrd/","n.","庭院、中庭","Employees often eat lunch in the courtyard.","員工常在中庭吃午餐。"],["load-bearing","/ˈloʊd ˌberɪŋ/","adj.","承重的","You cannot remove a load-bearing wall.","承重牆不能拆除。"]]});
